{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '192,234p' /Users/bonetto/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Task Group: HWE Bench GPT-5.6 benchmark integration and run operations\nscope: Use for configuring GPT-5.6 runs, publishing results, preserving checkpoints, storage cleanup, and clean shutdown.\napplies_to: cwd=/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament; reuse_rule=paths/configs are checkout-specific and runner behavior should be rechecked before use; process/checkpoint safeguards remain high value.\n\n## Task 1: Configure GPT-5.6 Sol/Terra/Luna high-only and site, partial\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-10T12-06-14-IIqv-gpt56_benchmark_integration_run_management.md (cwd=/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament, rollout_path=/Users/bonetto/.codex/sessions/2026/07/10/rollout-2026-07-10T09-06-14-019f4beb-d697-7f31-a3ac-0367c0a2db5b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T13:16:41+00:00, thread_id=019f4beb-d697-7f31-a3ac-0367c0a2db5b)\n\n### keywords\n\n- models-gpt56-preview.yaml, openai/gpt-5.6-sol, openai/gpt-5.6-terra, openai/gpt-5.6-luna, variant: high, watch_publish, d0886f5, core_pkg.sv\n\n## Task 2: Monitor, cleanup, and stop benchmark runs, success\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-10T12-06-14-IIqv-gpt56_benchmark_integration_run_management.md (cwd=/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament, rollout_path=/Users/bonetto/.codex/sessions/2026/07/10/rollout-2026-07-10T09-06-14-019f4beb-d697-7f31-a3ac-0367c0a2db5b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T13:16:41+00:00, thread_id=019f4beb-d697-7f31-a3ac-0367c0a2db5b)\n\n### keywords\n\n- No space left on device, /private/tmp/bench-*, .claude/bench-runs, summary_missing, sby, yosys-smtbmc, bitwuzla, PGID, df -h /private/tmp\n\n## User preferences\n\n- “gpt-5.6 (sol, terra, luna) (only high)” means exactly those variants with `variant: high`, no fast/pro or other efforts; also update both “our tournament and hwebench website.” [Task 1]\n- For “stats?” / “are we running?”, report processes, current round, best fitness, disk free, and publisher/janitor state. For “ok stop them,” stop coordinator and orphaned solver groups and verify none remain. [Task 2]\n- Before cleanup, inspect active processes/checkpoints; preserve `.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-*` and remove stale `/private/tmp/bench-*` trees only. [Task 2]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- Catalog IDs are `openai/gpt-5.6-{sol,terra,luna}`. `tools/bench/models-gpt56-preview.yaml` uses `provider: codex`, `model: gpt-5.6-*`, `variant: high`, `oauth: true`; website publishing is `python -m tools.site.watch_publish --poll-sec 30`. [Task 1]\n- Site build/report are `python -m tools.site.build` and `python -m tools.bench.report`; release-date chart commit `d0886f5` had successful Pages deployment and seven site tests. [Task 1]\n- Inspect with `ps -axo pid,ppid,pgid,etime,state,%cpu,%mem,command`, experiment `log.jsonl`, and `df -h /private/tmp`. Remove zero-iteration `summary_missing: true` rows and empty artifacts before rerun/publication. [Task 2]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Verilator rejects glob ordering when `core.sv` precedes typedefs in `core_pkg.sv` -> enumerate RTL and place `core_pkg.sv` first. Do baseline lint/formal preflight before paid rounds; `sby` may fail `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'click'`. [Task 1]\n- Standard runner recreates clones, so it cannot natively resume partial work -> preserve `.claude/bench-runs/...` and invoke remaining rounds in place. [Task 1]\n- Killing Python coordinator alone leaves detached `sby`, `yosys-smtbmc`, `bitwuzla` -> terminate PGIDs, then `ps`/`pgrep` recheck. Do not delete checkpoint directories during space recovery. [Task 2]\n\n# Task Group: Structural acrostic puzzle solving\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path.cwd()\nfor d in list(p.parents)[::-1]+[p]:\n    f=d/'AGENTS.md'\n    if f.exists():\n        print(str(f)+'\\\\n'+f.read_text())\nfor name in ['cores/AGENTS.md','cores/bench/AGENTS.md','cores/bench/experiments/AGENTS.md','cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/AGENTS.md','cores/bench/LESSONS.md','schemas/hypothesis.schema.json']:\n    f=Path(name)\n    if f.exists(): print(str(f)+'\\\\n'+f.read_text())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path.cwd()\nfor d in list(p.parents)[::-1]+[p]:\n    f=d/'AGENTS.md'\n    if f.exists():\n        print(str(f)+'\\\\n'+f.read_text())\nfor name in ['cores/AGENTS.md','cores/bench/AGENTS.md','cores/bench/experiments/AGENTS.md','cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/AGENTS.md','cores/bench/LESSONS.md','schemas/hypothesis.schema.json']:\n    f=Path(name)\n    if f.exists(): print(str(f)+'\\\\n'+f.read_text())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"cores/bench/LESSONS.md\n- 2026-09-06 hyp-20260906-002-r1s1 (improvement, +31.75%): Moving combinational DIV/REM off the single-cycle execute path into a shared blocking divider raised median Fmax 31.75% with no CoreMark cycle penalty because the timed region executed no DIV/REM, so the throughput gain depends on the workload's division frequency.\n- 2026-09-06 hyp-20260906-003-r1s2 (regression, +2.96%): Small BTBs still need timing and area headroom: this 16-entry full-width tagged predictor cut CoreMark cycles 6.13%, but a 3.35% median Fmax loss limited throughput gain to 2.96%, with total area reaching 10,377 LUT4 against a 10,000-LUT target.\n- 2026-09-06 hyp-20260906-001-r2s0 (regression, -5.98%): Replacing ALU case selection with registered one-hot masks and a balanced OR tree disrupted multiplier sharing (MULT36X36 count rose from 1 to 3) and left slower selector-to-EX/MEM paths critical, lowering median Fmax 5.98% despite unchanged arithmetic and CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-09-06 hyp-20260906-002-r2s1 (improvement, +0.85%): Routing the post-register DIV/REM result-bank mux into mem_stage.address blocks Yosys BRAM address-register absorption, so memory addresses must use the normal EX/MEM bank directly to avoid expansion from four block RAMs to 1,024 RAM16SDP4 blocks and placement failure.\n- 2026-09-06 hyp-20260906-003-r2s2 (regression, -7.39%): Registering BTB hit/counter metadata removed tag-read training feedback, but EX legality/alignment qualification and predictor payload write-enable fanout still cut median Fmax 13.07%, outweighing 6.14% fewer CoreMark cycles.\n\nschemas/hypothesis.schema.json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
