{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '150,178p' /Users/bonetto/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\nsed -n '1,240p' fpga/scripts/synth.tcl\nrg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' cores/bench .agents .codex 2>/dev/null\"","aggregated_output":"# Task Group: HWE Bench model-capability study planning\nscope: Use for HWE Bench paper framing, prospective model cohorts, runtime disclosure, and cost reporting.\napplies_to: cwd=/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament; reuse_rule=use as the current study-design intent unless the user changes the benchmark claim or budget.\n\n## Task 1: Reframe HWE Bench as a model-capability benchmark, success\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-09-05T17-38-53-5hEW-hwe_bench_model_capability_study_plan.md (cwd=/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament, rollout_path=/Users/bonetto/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T19-38-53-01a072a6-df12-7e61-a653-f14336ae4be6.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T19:00:14+00:00, thread_id=01a072a6-df12-7e61-a653-f14336ae4be6)\n\n### keywords\n\n- HWE Bench, ICLR, model capability, fixed benchmark contract, 15 rounds, 3 slots, CoreMark, V0 282.82, paper/iclr2027/main.tex\n\n## Task 2: Define three-repetition cohort and cost policy, success\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-09-05T17-38-53-5hEW-hwe_bench_model_capability_study_plan.md (cwd=/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament, rollout_path=/Users/bonetto/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T19-38-53-01a072a6-df12-7e61-a653-f14336ae4be6.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T19:00:14+00:00, thread_id=01a072a6-df12-7e61-a653-f14336ae4be6)\n\n### keywords\n\n- GPT-5.4, GPT-5.5, GPT-5.6 Sol, GPT-6 Astra, Kimi K3, Codex, OpenCode, sample standard deviation, models.json, STUDY_PLAN.md\n\n## User preferences\n\n- The user clarified this is “a benchmark” asking “How good can the models get” -> prioritize fair model comparisons under a fixed contract, not optimization-harness attribution. [Task 1]\n- Benchmark overfitting is acceptable; memory/search ablations are unnecessary, and a human baseline already exists -> do not add held-out workloads, harness ablations, or a new human study unless claims broaden. [Task 1]\n- Five runs are outside budget -> use three repetitions, show all endpoints, mean, and sample standard deviation; avoid fine-grained rankings. [Task 2]\n# Yosys synthesis script: build the Fmax-benchmark wrapper.\n#\n# $rtl_dir/*.sv is globbed dynamically (core_pkg.sv first for compilation-\n# unit-scope typedefs). Hypotheses are allowed to add/rename/delete\n# files inside $rtl_dir/, so a hardcoded list would silently break\n# restructuring hypotheses (the orchestrator would log them as\n# build_failed regardless of merit).\nyosys -import\n\nif {![info exists ::env(RTL_DIR)]} {\n    error \"synth.tcl requires the RTL_DIR env var (e.g. RTL_DIR=cores/v1/rtl).\"\n}\nset rtl_dir $::env(RTL_DIR)\n\nif {![info exists ::env(GEN_DIR)]} {\n    error \"synth.tcl requires the GEN_DIR env var (e.g. GEN_DIR=cores/v1/generated).\"\n}\nset gen_dir $::env(GEN_DIR)\n\n# Ordering: read core_pkg.sv first so its typedefs/localparams are\n# visible to subsequent files.\nread_verilog -sv \"$rtl_dir/core_pkg.sv\"\n\n# Then everything else under $rtl_dir/. glob -nocomplain handles the empty\n# case; we filter core_pkg.sv out to avoid double-include.\nforeach f [lsort [glob -nocomplain \"$rtl_dir/*.sv\"]] {\n    if {[file tail $f] == \"core_pkg.sv\"} { continue }\n    read_verilog -sv \"$f\"\n}\n\n# BENCH selects which fpga/core_bench*.sv to read. Defaults to\n# fpga/core_bench.sv (NRET=2 dual-channel). tools/eval/fpga.py overrides\n# to fpga/core_bench_si.sv when cores/<target>/core.yaml declares nret: 1.\n# Both files define a module named core_bench; only one is read per run.\nif {[info exists ::env(BENCH)]} {\n    set bench_sv $::env(BENCH)\n} else {\n    set bench_sv \"fpga/core_bench.sv\"\n}\nread_verilog -sv $bench_sv\n\nsynth_gowin -top core_bench -json $gen_dir/synth.json\n\nstat\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
