{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path.cwd()\nfor d in [*reversed(p.parents),p,p/'cores',p/'cores/bench',p/'cores/bench/experiments',p/'cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses']:\n f=d/'AGENTS.md'\n if f.is_file():\n  print(f'FILE {f}\\\\n{f.read_text()}')\nPY\nnl -ba /Users/bonetto/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '150,186p'\ngit status --short\nrg --files cores/bench/experiments cores/bench/test .tmp | head -80\"","aggregated_output":"   150\t# Task Group: HWE Bench model-capability study planning\n   151\tscope: Use for HWE Bench paper framing, prospective model cohorts, runtime disclosure, and cost reporting.\n   152\tapplies_to: cwd=/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament; reuse_rule=use as the current study-design intent unless the user changes the benchmark claim or budget.\n   153\t\n   154\t## Task 1: Reframe HWE Bench as a model-capability benchmark, success\n   155\t\n   156\t### rollout_summary_files\n   157\t\n   158\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-05T17-38-53-5hEW-hwe_bench_model_capability_study_plan.md (cwd=/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament, rollout_path=/Users/bonetto/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T19-38-53-01a072a6-df12-7e61-a653-f14336ae4be6.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T19:00:14+00:00, thread_id=01a072a6-df12-7e61-a653-f14336ae4be6)\n   159\t\n   160\t### keywords\n   161\t\n   162\t- HWE Bench, ICLR, model capability, fixed benchmark contract, 15 rounds, 3 slots, CoreMark, V0 282.82, paper/iclr2027/main.tex\n   163\t\n   164\t## Task 2: Define three-repetition cohort and cost policy, success\n   165\t\n   166\t### rollout_summary_files\n   167\t\n   168\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-05T17-38-53-5hEW-hwe_bench_model_capability_study_plan.md (cwd=/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament, rollout_path=/Users/bonetto/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T19-38-53-01a072a6-df12-7e61-a653-f14336ae4be6.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T19:00:14+00:00, thread_id=01a072a6-df12-7e61-a653-f14336ae4be6)\n   169\t\n   170\t### keywords\n   171\t\n   172\t- GPT-5.4, GPT-5.5, GPT-5.6 Sol, GPT-6 Astra, Kimi K3, Codex, OpenCode, sample standard deviation, models.json, STUDY_PLAN.md\n   173\t\n   174\t## User preferences\n   175\t\n   176\t- The user clarified this is “a benchmark” asking “How good can the models get” -> prioritize fair model comparisons under a fixed contract, not optimization-harness attribution. [Task 1]\n   177\t- Benchmark overfitting is acceptable; memory/search ablations are unnecessary, and a human baseline already exists -> do not add held-out workloads, harness ablations, or a new human study unless claims broaden. [Task 1]\n   178\t- Five runs are outside budget -> use three repetitions, show all endpoints, mean, and sample standard deviation; avoid fine-grained rankings. [Task 2]\n   179\t- Use Codex for new GPT runs and OpenCode for open-source runs; historical cost is unreliable -> retain runtime labels/confounding and report only verifiable new-run cost. [Task 2]\n   180\t\n   181\t## Reusable knowledge\n   182\t\n   183\t- Central question: CPU performance produced under fixed architectural contract/evaluation budget, and its relationship to verified model release date. Say “open-ended,” not literally unsaturable. Keep fixture, constraints, evaluator, candidate limits, and 15 rounds × 3 slots fixed. [Task 1][Task 2]\n   184\t- Planned matrix: existing GPT-5.4/5.5 OpenCode cohorts; new GPT-5.6 Sol/GPT-6 Astra via Codex at highest verified effort; Kimi K3 via OpenCode; three repetitions each. Equal proposal budgets do not prove equal inference compute. [Task 2]\n   185\t- Plot verified release date, treat reasoning variants as configurations rather than releases, show every endpoint plus mean/sample SD, and preserve raw usage. OAuth/subscription parsers returning `$0` are unavailable billing, not measured spend. [Task 2]\n   186\t\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\ncores/bench/experiments/progress.png\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\ncores/bench/test/test_ex_result_banks.py\n.tmp/predictor-supplemental-6k-gvvrkbrq/build.log\n.tmp/predictor-supplemental-6k-gvvrkbrq/sim.log\n.tmp/predictor-supplemental-6k-gvvrkbrq/result.json\n.tmp/predictor-supplemental-6k-gvvrkbrq/bench/programs/crt0.S\n.tmp/predictor-supplemental-6k-gvvrkbrq/bench/programs/coremark/cygwin/core_portme.mak\n.tmp/stateless-r3s2/cores/bench/core.yaml\n.tmp/predictor-supplemental-6k-gvvrkbrq/bench/programs/coremark/zephyr/module.yml\n.tmp/predictor-supplemental-6k-gvvrkbrq/bench/programs/coremark/coremark.h\n.tmp/predictor-supplemental-6k-gvvrkbrq/bench/programs/coremark/barebones/core_portme.mak\n.tmp/predictor-supplemental-6k-gvvrkbrq/bench/programs/coremark/barebones/core_portme.c\n.tmp/predictor-supplemental-6k-gvvrkbrq/bench/programs/coremark/barebones/ee_printf.c\n.tmp/predictor-supplemental-6k-gvvrkbrq/bench/programs/coremark/barebones/cvt.c\n.tmp/predictor-supplemental-6k-gvvrkbrq/bench/programs/coremark/barebones/core_portme.h\n.tmp/predictor-supplemental-6k-gvvrkbrq/bench/programs/coremark/linux/core_portme.mak\n.tmp/predictor-supplemental-6k-gvvrkbrq/bench/programs/coremark/core_main.c\n.tmp/stateless-r3s2/cores/bench/obj_dir/Vcore__ALL.cpp\n.tmp/stateless-r3s2/cores/bench/obj_dir/Vcore___024unit.h\n.tmp/stateless-r3s2/cores/bench/obj_dir/Vcore__ALL.o\n.tmp/stateless-r3s2/cores/bench/obj_dir/Vcore__ALL.a\n.tmp/stateless-r3s2/cores/bench/obj_dir/Vcore_classes.mk\n.tmp/stateless-r3s2/cores/bench/obj_dir/Vcore___024unit__0__Slow.cpp\n.tmp/stateless-r3s2/cores/bench/obj_dir/Vcore___024root__Slow.cpp\n.tmp/stateless-r3s2/cores/bench/obj_dir/verilated.d\n.tmp/stateless-r3s2/cores/bench/obj_dir/Vcore__ConstPool__0__Slow.cpp\n.tmp/stateless-r3s2/cores/bench/o