{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport subprocess,json\nr=subprocess.run(['rg','\\\"category\\\"\\\\\\\\s*:\\\\\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"','cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'],text=True,capture_output=True,check=True)\nfor line in r.stdout.splitlines():\n x=json.loads(line)\n print(json.dumps({k:x.get(k) for k in ['id','title','outcome','fitness','delta_pct','fmax_mhz','cycles','lesson']},indent=2))\n if x['id']=='hyp-20260906-002-r5s1':\n  note=x.get('implementation_notes','')\n  i=note.find('All three final routed')\n  print(note[i:i+3000])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260906-002-r1s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Separate bounded multicycle division from the single-cycle execute path\",\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 372.62,\n  \"delta_pct\": 31.75,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 167.36,\n  \"cycles\": 4491485,\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-06 hyp-20260906-002-r1s1 (improvement, +31.75%): Moving combinational DIV/REM off the single-cycle execute path into a shared blocking divider raised median Fmax 31.75% with no CoreMark cycle penalty because the timed region executed no DIV/REM, so the throughput gain depends on the workload's division frequency.\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260906-002-r2s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Retiming divide writeback into a separate EX/MEM result bank\",\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 375.78,\n  \"delta_pct\": 0.85,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 168.78,\n  \"cycles\": 4491485,\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-06 hyp-20260906-002-r2s1 (improvement, +0.85%): Routing the post-register DIV/REM result-bank mux into mem_stage.address blocks Yosys BRAM address-register absorption, so memory addresses must use the normal EX/MEM bank directly to avoid expansion from four block RAMs to 1,024 RAM16SDP4 blocks and placement failure.\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260906-002-r3s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Two radix-4 quotient stages per divider clock\",\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 159.15,\n  \"delta_pct\": -57.65,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 71.48,\n  \"cycles\": 4491485,\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-06 hyp-20260906-002-r3s1 (regression, -57.65%): Halving divider quotient stages does not guarantee better mapped timing: two radix-4 stages in div_unit.sv cascaded 35-bit trial subtraction and underflow-driven masked-OR selection into terminal sign correction, yielding a reported ~14 ns completion path with unchanged CoreMark cycles.\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260906-002-r4s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Retime divider finalization using a narrow request-edge prefix\",\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 382.48,\n  \"delta_pct\": 1.78,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 171.79,\n  \"cycles\": 4491485,\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-06 hyp-20260906-002-r4s1 (improvement, +1.78%): Precomputing the first four restoring bits with a narrow request-edge prefix in div_unit.sv separates sign correction from the wide recurrence by using registered quotient_q/remainder_q, improving fitness without extending the eight-clock response schedule.\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260906-002-r5s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Separate pipeline payload storage from bubble and divide control\",\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 409.8,\n  \"delta_pct\": 7.14,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 184.06,\n  \"cycles\": 4491485,\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-06 hyp-20260906-002-r5s1 (improvement, +7.14%): Separating ID/EX and EX/MEM payload capture from bubble/flush and divide-completion control removed those decisions from wide data/reset/enable cones, raising reported median Fmax 7.14% with unchanged CoreMark cycles while requiring zero control on invalid entries and full payload/control retention during memory stalls.\"\n}\nAll three final routed critical-path reports were inspected:\n\n| Seed | Fmax MHz | Reported worst path | Total ns | Logic / routing ns |\n| --- | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | 184.06 | EX/MEM rd[0], through forwarding selection and JALR target, to IF pc[1] | 5.43 | 3.06 / 2.38 |\n| 2 | 191.13 | Wrapper instruction stimulus lfsr[20] to ID rs2_val[3] | 5.23 | 2.61 / 2.63 |\n| 3 | 179.89 | EX/MEM rd[0], through forwarding selection and JALR target, to IF pc[1] | 5.56 | 3.06 / 2.50 |\n\nFigures are rounded independently by nextpnr. Tools are Yosys 0.64 (`d8dab5b32666564eca8e18f412973853ce006e61`) and nextpnr `0.10-45-g98c18d7f`. The requested standalone lint used Verilator 5.047; the unit and cosimulation gates used the installed Verilator 5.046 with the Conda Python environment containing cocotb and YAML. The eight Yosys array-to-register warnings originate in the unchanged divider.\n\nTiming remains a reported tool estimate. Prior result-bank experiments observed missing LUT3 bank-selector IOPATH arcs and omitted MEM/WB result endpoints in detailed exports. This run inspects all three unchanged routed gate reports and connectivity, but does not recharacterize those missing arcs or establish complete bank-to-forwarding/MEM/WB physical timing. No omitted arc is treated as zero delay; no timing model, constraint, or evaluation criterion was changed. The new critical paths do not prove that divider, multiplier, or other forwarding paths have timing margin.\n\nThe checked-in evaluator uses aggregate **2 KB, -O3, ITERATIONS=10**, whereas the requested supplemental run uses aggregate **6 KB**. The evaluator and its expected CRCs remain unchanged. The separate 6 KB ELF was built from identical benchmark sources with the existing Makefile options `COREMARK_SIZE=6000 COREMARK_OPT=-O3`. Starting and final RTL were freshly simulated with the exact same ELF per size and identical `--bench --istall --dstall` flags/default deterministic seed.\n\n| Workload | Start / stop markers, both RTL versions | Starting cycles | Final cycles | Starting / final iter/sec |\n| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Evaluator 2 KB | 15,801 / 4,507,286 | 4,491,485 | 4,491,485 | 382.48 / 409.80 |\n| Supplemental 6 KB | 56,393 / 32,893,064 | 32,836,671 | 32,836,671 | 52.32 / 56.05 |\n\nRates use the recorded starting 171.79 MHz and measured final 184.06 MHz; starting FPGA routing was not rerun. Both versions reach EBREAK, report no OOB access, provide valid marker brackets, and produce identical UART output for each workload. Both include the literal `Correct operation validated.` and ten iterations. Evaluator CRCs are seedcrc=e9f5, crclist=e714, crcmatrix=1fd7, crcstate=8e3a, crcfinal=fcaf. The separately verified **6 KB CRCs are seedcrc=8a02, crclist=d4b0, crcmatrix=be52, crcstate=5e47, crcfinal=5949**. The unchanged UART description says -O2; the actual compile commands use -O3.\n\nAll build artifacts and scratch contract copies are under the configured TMPDIR:\n`/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-to\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
