{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=[json.loads(s) for s in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines() if s.strip()]\nfor r in rows:\n    if r.get('id') in ['hyp-20260906-003-r4s2','hyp-20260906-003-r6s2','hyp-20260906-001-r6s0']:\n        print('\\\\n'+r['id'])\n        for para in r.get('implementation_notes','').split('\\\\n\\\\n'):\n            if any(w in para.lower() for w in ['jalr','profile','critical','failure','failed','broken']):\n                print(para+'\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"\nhyp-20260906-003-r4s2\nOnly four RTL files changed: `core_pkg.sv`, `if_stage.sv`, `id_stage.sv`, and\n`ex_stage.sv`. IF predecodes raw `imem_data` for opcode 0x6f, aligned PC, and\ninstruction bit 21 clear. The sign-extended J displacement feeds one full-width\nPC-relative adder; PC+4 remains independent. Both wrap modulo 2^32.\n`imem_addr` remains directly assigned from the PC register. Branches, JALR,\nand all other opcodes predict sequentially.\n\nID/EX registers `dec_is_jump && !in.early_jal` as `jump_needs_redirect`, using\nthe existing reset/flush and hold policy. Invalid fetches retain the existing\ndecoded-NOP payload policy; no invalid-fetch-wide reset was added. EX changes\nonly the jump term in its redirect predicate. Architectural jump controls,\nPC+4 link results, resolved RVFI targets, alignment traps, and JALR forwarding\nand bit-zero clearing remain intact. The divider, result banks, registered\ndmem address, forwarding, hazard unit, retirement logic, and nret=1 IO are\nunchanged. There is no predictor state, training, saved target, target/direction\ncomparison, fallback repair mux, or new EX-advance/div_wait qualification.\n\nTests add direct IF and ID coverage and extend the existing pipeline and EX\nresult-bank tests without removing their assertions. Coverage includes signed\nJAL displacements and extremes, full-address carry/wrap, every non-JAL opcode,\nalignment, changing instructions during holds, reset/redirect priority,\nconsecutive/self JALs, x0/x1/x5 links and forwarding, imem stalls, an 18-cycle\nolder memory hold, preceding divider waits, load-use bubbles, misaligned-JAL\ncontinuation, forwarded JALR, and older redirects killing younger JAL/store/divide.\nPipeline tests compare complete RVFI traces against the unchanged ISS and\ncheck accepted memory transactions and divider launches separately.\n\nAn opt-in `test_coremark_profile.py` observes accepted early JALs directly,\nusing the unchanged ELF and the C++ harness's exact xorshift stall sequence.\nIt adds no RTL counters and does not replace any evaluator gate. The final\nprofile matches the unchanged C++ simulation's markers exactly:\n\n- Requested `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv\n  +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: PASS, no warnings.\n- `make test TARGET=bench`: PASS, 10 runners; the opt-in profile is skipped\n  by default and separately PASS when enabled. Includes real and ALTOPS\n  arithmetic/result-bank tests and all 25 pipeline cases.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=4 bash formal/run_all.sh`:\n  **PASS, 53 passed, 0 failed**, using the unchanged single-channel wrapper\n  and configuration. Both local formal invocations passed. No formal\n  counterexample or formal fix attempt occurred. All final generated checks\n  have DONE (PASS), and all 14 staged RTL files match the submitted RTL.\n- Unchanged `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1`: PASS, selftest and CoreMark.\n- Unchanged `make fpga TARGET=bench NRET=1 BENCH=fpga/core_bench_si.sv`:\n  completed all three seeds, CRC/UART, OOB, and marker-window gates.\n- `git diff --check`: PASS. No evaluator, other core, or core.yaml edits.\n\nScratch copies and generated evidence are under\n`$TMPDIR/early-jal-hove0D` (the run's configured TMPDIR, outside other cores).\nEvidence includes `formal-output.log`, `unit-tests.log`, `profile-tests.log`,\n`coremark-profile.json`, `cosim-gate.log`, `fpga-gate.log`,\n`cores/bench/generated/pnr_seed*/nextpnr.log`, `timing-summary.json`,\n`workload-validation.json`, the individual benchmark logs, and\n`sixk/build.log`. `verified-source-sha256.json` verifies 169 staged RTL,\ntest, and unchanged contract source files against the worktree. This\nrequested notes file is at the worktree root per instruction 5.\nOrchestrator acceptance remains separate from these local results.\n\n\n\nhyp-20260906-001-r6s0\nImplemented the JALR alignment precomputation hypothesis. All local correctness\ngates passed, but the measured fitness **regressed 8.89%, from 409.80 to 373.37**.\nMedian reported Fmax fell from 184.06 to **167.70 MHz** with unchanged benchmark\ncycles. The estimated four percent improvement was not observed. Local gate\nsuccess is separate from orchestrator acceptance.\n\nOnly `cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv` changed in RTL. It computes three independent\nsum-bit-1 expressions from `in.rs1_val`, `fwd_ex_mem`, and `fwd_mem_wb` using\n`base[1] ^ in.imm[1] ^ (base[0] & in.imm[0])`. A separate one-bit case mux uses\nthe existing forwarding encoding: 1 selects EX/MEM, 2 selects MEM/WB, and both\n0 and 3 default to the ID/EX value. Both JALR target bit 1 and its misalignment\npredicate consume that selected bit directly. The original full-width\n`rs1 + in.imm` still supplies target bits [31:2], including the carry from the\nlow bits and modulo-2^32 wraparound. Target bit 0 remains cleared. No full-width\nadder was replicated and no predicate is computed from already-forwarded rs1.\n\n`test_pipeline.py` adds register-file, EX/MEM, MEM/WB, competing-writer, x0,\nload-use, and divider-result JALR cases with aligned/misaligned sums and negative\nimmediates. Each runs with zero-wait and deterministic random bus stalls.\nTests verify actual forwarding selections, freshest-writer priority, suppressed\ntrap links, discarded stores, consecutive redirects, one-cycle ordinary/divide\nconsumer spacing, the existing two-cycle load-use spacing, and two-cycle target\nretirement spacing. Directed 12-cycle overlapping imem/dmem holds exercise\nrepeated aligned redirects and repeatedly suppressed misaligned redirects while\nMEM/WB retains the needed source. Per-cycle assertions preserve fetch redirect\npriority, all existing bank/metadata holds, and accepted memory effects. Complete\nretirement streams are compared through the unchanged ISS and comparator,\nincluding PC continuity and gap-free order.\n\n- Requested Verilator lint command: **PASS, no warnings**.\n- Unchanged `make test TARGET=bench`: **PASS, 9 runners / 148 cocotb cases**,\n  including 24 pipeline cases, 7 EX cases in each arithmetic mode, and all\n  existing ALU, decoder, register-file, and ID checks. No failures or skips.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=4 bash formal/run_all.sh`:\n  **PASS, 53 passed / 0 failed on the first invocation**. The script\n  auto-selected the unchanged nret=1 wrapper and configuration. Zero formal\n  fix attempts; no counterexample. This is the required ALTOPS gate. Deep\n  arithmetic formal was not run because multiplier/divider arithmetic did\n  not change.\n- Unchanged `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1`: **PASS, selftest and CoreMark**.\n- Unchanged `make fpga TARGET=bench NRET=1 BENCH=fpga/core_bench_si.sv`:\n  **PASS, all three placements and CRC/UART/OOB/marker checks**, with the\n  performance regression reported above.\n- `git diff --check`: **PASS**. SHA-256 verification covers 227 staged source\n  and contract files. Every formal-staged RTL file matches the submitted\n  source; the fresh baseline simulation sources match HEAD.\n\nAll three complete final routed critical-path reports were inspected:\n\nEvidence directory:\n`/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/astra-max-20260905/bench-runs/gpt-6-astra_max-rep2/.tmp/hyp-r6s0-jalr-mivgf56j`\n\nIt contains formal-output.log, unit-tests.log and all nine result XMLs,\ncosim-output.log, fpga-output.log, the three original nextpnr logs and routed\nnetlists, jalr-premap.json, mapped-jalr-connectivity.json, timing-seed1.json/SDF,\ntiming-arc-audit.json, workload-comparison.json, all four baseline/candidate\nbenchmark logs, sixk/build.log, and verified-source-sha256.json. All launched\nvalidation commands have completed.\n\n\n\nhyp-20260906-003-r6s2\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
