{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '192,232p' /Users/bonetto/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Task Group: HWE Bench GPT-5.6 benchmark integration and run operations\nscope: Use for configuring GPT-5.6 runs, publishing results, preserving checkpoints, storage cleanup, and clean shutdown.\napplies_to: cwd=/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament; reuse_rule=paths/configs are checkout-specific and runner behavior should be rechecked before use; process/checkpoint safeguards remain high value.\n\n## Task 1: Configure GPT-5.6 Sol/Terra/Luna high-only and site, partial\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-10T12-06-14-IIqv-gpt56_benchmark_integration_run_management.md (cwd=/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament, rollout_path=/Users/bonetto/.codex/sessions/2026/07/10/rollout-2026-07-10T09-06-14-019f4beb-d697-7f31-a3ac-0367c0a2db5b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T13:16:41+00:00, thread_id=019f4beb-d697-7f31-a3ac-0367c0a2db5b)\n\n### keywords\n\n- models-gpt56-preview.yaml, openai/gpt-5.6-sol, openai/gpt-5.6-terra, openai/gpt-5.6-luna, variant: high, watch_publish, d0886f5, core_pkg.sv\n\n## Task 2: Monitor, cleanup, and stop benchmark runs, success\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-10T12-06-14-IIqv-gpt56_benchmark_integration_run_management.md (cwd=/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament, rollout_path=/Users/bonetto/.codex/sessions/2026/07/10/rollout-2026-07-10T09-06-14-019f4beb-d697-7f31-a3ac-0367c0a2db5b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T13:16:41+00:00, thread_id=019f4beb-d697-7f31-a3ac-0367c0a2db5b)\n\n### keywords\n\n- No space left on device, /private/tmp/bench-*, .claude/bench-runs, summary_missing, sby, yosys-smtbmc, bitwuzla, PGID, df -h /private/tmp\n\n## User preferences\n\n- “gpt-5.6 (sol, terra, luna) (only high)” means exactly those variants with `variant: high`, no fast/pro or other efforts; also update both “our tournament and hwebench website.” [Task 1]\n- For “stats?” / “are we running?”, report processes, current round, best fitness, disk free, and publisher/janitor state. For “ok stop them,” stop coordinator and orphaned solver groups and verify none remain. [Task 2]\n- Before cleanup, inspect active processes/checkpoints; preserve `.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-*` and remove stale `/private/tmp/bench-*` trees only. [Task 2]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- Catalog IDs are `openai/gpt-5.6-{sol,terra,luna}`. `tools/bench/models-gpt56-preview.yaml` uses `provider: codex`, `model: gpt-5.6-*`, `variant: high`, `oauth: true`; website publishing is `python -m tools.site.watch_publish --poll-sec 30`. [Task 1]\n- Site build/report are `python -m tools.site.build` and `python -m tools.bench.report`; release-date chart commit `d0886f5` had successful Pages deployment and seven site tests. [Task 1]\n- Inspect with `ps -axo pid,ppid,pgid,etime,state,%cpu,%mem,command`, experiment `log.jsonl`, and `df -h /private/tmp`. Remove zero-iteration `summary_missing: true` rows and empty artifacts before rerun/publication. [Task 2]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Verilator rejects glob ordering when `core.sv` precedes typedefs in `core_pkg.sv` -> enumerate RTL and place `core_pkg.sv` first. Do baseline lint/formal preflight before paid rounds; `sby` may fail `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'click'`. [Task 1]\n- Standard runner recreates clones, so it cannot natively resume partial work -> preserve `.claude/bench-runs/...` and invoke remaining rounds in place. [Task 1]\n- Killing Python coordinator alone leaves detached `sby`, `yosys-smtbmc`, `bitwuzla` -> terminate PGIDs, then `ps`/`pgrep` recheck. Do not delete checkpoint directories during space recovery. [Task 2]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
