a-max-20260905/bench-runs/gpt-6-astra_max-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260906-003-r6s2/formal/last_run-87052.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/astra-max-20260905/bench-runs/gpt-6-astra_max-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260906-003-r6s2/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-87052/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 6}\n22:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260906-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Single-entry backedge target prediction with decode validation\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current core fetches sequentially and loses one fetch/decode slot on\\nan advancing taken branch because IF/ID is combinational. Prior predictor\\nexperiments establish useful cycle savings but very little timing budget:\\nr2s2's 16-entry BTB saved 6.135% of cycles but lost 13.074% median Fmax,\\nwith EX qualification driving wide predictor write enables; r5s2's static\\nbackward predictor saved 4.05% of cycles but lost 14.98% median Fmax.\\nRemoving state or narrowing squash fanout alone did not solve timing.\\nr6s2 moved validation to MEM and failed the unchanged liveness check,\\nso its longer recovery must not be assumed viable.\\n\\nTry a much smaller learned predictor for repeated loop backedges. A\\nsingle resident branch removes the indexed table read and broad write\\nfanout. A cached displacement lets decode certify the target without\\nputting instruction predecode or a new target adder in fetch, or a\\nfull actual-versus-predicted PC comparison in EX. This is a new timing\\ntradeoff, not evidence that a smaller predictor necessarily routes faster.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current core fetches sequentially and loses one fetch/decode slot on\\nan advancing taken branch because IF/ID is combinational. Prior predictor\\nexperiments establish useful cycle savings but very little timing budget:\\nr2s2's 16-entry BTB saved 6.135% of cycles but lost 13.074% median Fmax,\\nwith EX qualification driving wide predictor write enables; r5s2's static\\nbackward predictor saved 4.05% of cycles but lost 14.98% median Fmax.\\nRemoving state or narrowing squash fanout alone did not solve timing.\\nr6s2 moved validation to MEM and failed the unchanged liveness check,\\nso its longer recovery must not be assumed viable.\\n\\nTry a much smaller learned predictor for repeated loop backedges. A\\nsingle resident branch removes the indexed table read and broad write\\nfanout. A cached displacement lets decode certify the target without\\nputting instruction predecode or a new target adder in fetch, or a\\nfull actual-versus-predicted PC comparison in EX. This is a new timing\\ntradeoff, not evidence that a smaller predictor necessarily routes faster.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add one fully tagged last-taken-backedge target entry. It contains valid,\\nsource PC[31:2], target[31:2], and the exact B displacement bits [12:1]:\\n73 logical state bits before constant-bit optimization. A lookup hit\\nrequires valid, word-aligned fetch PC, and equality of all source-PC\\nbits [31:2]. On a hit predict the stored full-width aligned target;\\notherwise predict full-width PC+4. Use no direction counter, indexed\\narray, return stack, or separate jump predictor. Only an accepted legal,\\ntaken conditional branch with negative displacement, aligned source PC,\\nand aligned target can replace the entry. Not-taken branches, forward\\nbranches, and jumps leave it unchanged. It therefore retains a hot\\ninner-loop backedge across intervening non-backedge control transfers.\\nNested backedges can evict one another; cold starts and loop exits cost\\nordinary EX repairs. No address-range truncation or workload PC constants\\nare permitted. Addition remains modulo 2^32, including page crossings.\\n\\nLookup and target selection depend only on registered PC and entry\\ncontents. Keep imem_addr directly driven by the PC register. Select the\\nraw lookup result in the PC data mux, and apply it only on actual fetch\\nacceptance into ID/EX; do not put acceptance, flush, or div_wait in the\\nprediction-select data cone. Reset and existing EX repair retain priority\\nover prediction. Hold fetch on ordinary load-use, bus, and divider stalls.\\nA prediction never squashes the instruction that produced it.\\n\\nCarry prediction_used and the cached displacement snapshot with the\\naccepting IF/ID instruction. Simultaneous lookup/update consumes the\\npre-edge entry, with no update bypass. In ID, certify a predicted target\\nonly if the CURRENT instruction decodes as a legal conditional branch\\nand its complete B displacement equals the saved displacement. The\\nsource-PC tag already matched the exact accepted PC, and training wrote\\nsource, target, and displacement coherently, so this equality proves the\\npredicted target equals this instruction's architectural branch target.\\nIt needs only immediate-bit comparison, not another PC-relative adder.\\nChanges in branch condition or source registers do not invalidate that\\nproof; EX must evaluate the current condition using forwarded operands.\\nRegister prediction_used, certified_backedge, and the repair polarity\\nwith ID/EX. Keep the architectural branch_op unchanged. For a certified\\nprediction, fold inversion of the outcome into the registered branch\\nrepair polarity, as in the earlier decode-folded comparator design.\\n\\nKeep recovery in EX and specify all three cases explicitly:\\n(1) No consumed prediction: retain the existing branch/jump redirect\\nand target-alignment behavior.\\n(2) Certified backedge: redirect only when its condition is false, to\\nPC+4; a taken outcome has no flush or bubble.\\n(3) Consumed but uncertified prediction: force repair to the current\\ninstruction's actual architectural next PC, for EVERY instruction class.\\nThat includes changed branch displacements, JAL/JALR, ordinary ALU,\\nload/store, DIV/REM, illegal encodings, and alignment traps. Use the\\nexisting PC+4 trap continuation and suppress trapped jump link writes.\\nThis conservative stale-entry repair needs no full predicted-PC field\\nor full-PC mismatch comparator in EX. A stale branch's actual outcome\\nstill selects target versus fall-through correctly; stale jumps use\\nthe current forwarded target. Keep this exceptional target selection\\nseparate from the common certified-exit PC+4 and ordinary redirect paths.\\n\\nQualify repair with valid and reset, retaining the existing level-style\\nEX repair behavior through holds. A held owner may repeatedly request\\nthe same repair; it must retain its operands and prediction flags until\\nadvancement. Do not add a generic EX-accept/div_wait gate to the common\\nbranch repair cone. In particular, an uncertified prediction on DIV/REM\\nmust not flush that owner or cancel its divide: existing divider-hold\\npriority retains ID/EX until completion, then the repair clears the\\nyounger slot on the accepting edge. Memory holds similarly defer owner\\nadvancement. Repairs override unavailable imem. Flush only the younger\\ncombinational fetch/decode slot, preserving the current recovery depth.\\n\\nStage predictor writes independently of recovery. Register a one-cycle\\ntrain_pending pulse when the qualifying backward branch actually enters\\nEX/MEM, using valid, legality, alignment, taken outcome, and !stall.\\nClear that pulse on every other clock, including holds and bubbles.\\nOn the following edge the predictor writes the coherent source, target,\\nand displacement from the existing EX/MEM pc, branch_target, and instr\\npayload. Those fields were captured on the same edge as train_pending;\\nnonblocking update semantics preserve their association on the write\\nedge. Reuse these payload fields instead of adding another wide training\\nbank. Only registered train_pending enables entry writes, with no live\\nEX comparator, resident-entry match, or memory-ready signal in that\\nwrite-enable cone. Each accepted branch trains once even when subsequent\\npipeline work stalls. Reset cancels pending training and clears entry\\nvalidity; inactive uninitialized entry payload cannot affect a miss.\\n\\nPreserve the winner's independent pipeline payload capture and narrow\\ncontrol/valid squashes. Hold accepted prediction metadata with its owner;\\ninvalid entries have inert repair/training controls. Preserve the decoder,\\narithmetic, divider completion bank, retained WB forwarding data, direct\\nregistered dmem address, actual RVFI pc_next, and nret=1 external ports.\\nThis experiment changes only backedge prediction and its integration.\\n\\nEstimate 2% higher fitness with low confidence. The explicit working\\nassumption is 2.5% fewer marker-window cycles with at most 0.5% median\\nFmax loss, yielding about 2.05% net gain. This is a forecast, not a\\nmeasurement; the one-entry coverage may be too small. Against 184.06 MHz\\nand 409.80 iter/sec, a 2.5% cycle reduction breaks even near 179.46 MHz.\\nCount useful hits, loop-exit/stale repairs, and backedge replacements\\ninside the existing timing markers. Run unchanged lint, unit, formal\\nincluding liveness, cosim, CRC/UART, OOB, marker, resource, and three-seed\\nFPGA gates. Inspect all routed seeds for lookup-to-PC, repair-to-squash,\\nand training-enable timing, including unchanged paths displaced by\\nrouting. Keep evaluator fitness authoritative and any separately built\\n6 KB measurement distinct, as prior notes document a fixture discrepancy.\\nDo not change any evaluator, formal bound, other core, or hard invariant.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the single fully tagged backedge entry with PC-only lookup,\\nfull-address target storage, displacement snapshot, valid-only\\nreset, and atomic writes from registered training information.\\nSpecify pre-edge read/write behavior and no resident-state training\\nfeedback. A miss must not expose uninitialized payload as a prediction.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend IF/ID with prediction_used and cached B displacement. Extend\\nID/EX with the small certified-prediction and repair-polarity flags.\\nDo not add a 32-bit predicted next PC or change retirement width.\\nReuse existing EX/MEM source-PC, instruction, and branch-target fields\\nfor the staged training payload.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select the raw entry hit/target for accepted fetch advances and\\nexport the exact consumed lookup snapshot. Preserve directly\\nregistered imem addressing, reset/EX-repair priority, hold behavior,\\nand invalid fetch suppression without putting handshake qualification\\ninto the prediction target-select data path.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Validate predicted backedges against current legal branch decode and\\nexact B displacement; capture the certified flag and folded repair\\npolarity with the instruction. Preserve architectural decode controls,\\nfull metadata holds, independent payload capture, and control-zero\\ninvalid/flush behavior.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement ordinary, certified-backedge, and uncertified-hit recovery\\nwhile preserving architectural resolution, traps, links, and forwarding.\\nKeep EX recovery and existing hold priority, including stale predictions\\non dividing owners. Generate a registered one-cycle training pulse only\\nfor accepted legal aligned taken backedges; reuse the associated\\nEX/MEM payload for the following edge's table write. Preserve direct\\nmemory-address and divider-result bank ownership.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire PC-only predictor lookup, fetch snapshots, the EX training pulse,\\nand existing EX/MEM payload into the predictor. Retain the existing EX\\nrepair connection and all external imem/dmem and channel-0 RVFI ports.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_branch_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for all source/tag and target bits, displacement\\nassociation, cold misses, overwrites by competing backedges, valid-only\\nreset, canceled pending writes, pre-edge lookup/write collisions, and\\nonce-per-accepted-owner training across holds. Verify full-address\\npage-crossing and wraparound cases without adding benchmark-specific PCs.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Verify zero-bubble warm backedges and one-slot loop-exit recovery,\\nnested-loop replacement, and stale hits after changing displacement,\\nopcode, condition, or registers. Include legal/misaligned JAL/JALR,\\nillegal instructions, ordinary ALU, loads/stores, and DIV/REM at a\\nformerly cached branch PC. Exercise load forwarding, long dmem holds,\\ndivider waits, imem unavailability, reset, and consecutive repairs.\\nCompare full RVFI against the unchanged ISS and separately monitor\\naccepted memory writes and divider launches for wrong-path effects.\\nAdd optional marker-window predictor event counts only in the unit\\ntest harness; preserve every existing correctness assertion.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_id_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Update input packing and check displacement certification, changed\\nbranch conditions, repair polarity, full metadata retention, invalid\\ncontrol clearing, and independent payload capture during squashes.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_ex_result_banks.py\", \"description\": \"Update ID/EX layout and default new prediction flags to no prediction\\nin existing tests. Add held and completing divide-owner cases with\\nuncertified predictions, retaining all current result-bank, forwarding,\\nmemory-address, reset, and exact arithmetic assertions.\\n\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the single fully tagged backedge entry with PC-only lookup,\\nfull-address target storage, displacement snapshot, valid-only\\nreset, and atomic writes from registered training information.\\nSpecify pre-edge read/write behavior and no resident-state training\\nfeedback. A miss must not expose uninitialized payload as a prediction.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend IF/ID with prediction_used and cached B displacement. Extend\\nID/EX with the small certified-prediction and repair-polarity flags.\\nDo not add a 32-bit predicted next PC or change retirement width.\\nReuse existing EX/MEM source-PC, instruction, and branch-target fields\\nfor the staged training payload.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select the raw entry hit/target for accepted fetch advances and\\nexport the exact consumed lookup snapshot. Preserve directly\\nregistered imem addressing, reset/EX-repair priority, hold behavior,\\nand invalid fetch suppression without putting handshake qualification\\ninto the prediction target-select data path.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Validate predicted backedges against current legal branch decode and\\nexact B displacement; capture the certified flag and folded repair\\npolarity with the instruction. Preserve architectural decode controls,\\nfull metadata holds, independent payload capture, and control-zero\\ninvalid/flush behavior.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement ordinary, certified-backedge, and uncertified-hit recovery\\nwhile preserving architectural resolution, traps, links, and forwarding.\\nKeep EX recovery and existing hold priority, including stale predictions\\non dividing owners. Generate a registered one-cycle training pulse only\\nfor accepted legal aligned taken backedges; reuse the associated\\nEX/MEM payload for the following edge's table write. Preserve direct\\nmemory-address and divider-result bank ownership.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire PC-only predictor lookup, fetch snapshots, the EX training pulse,\\nand existing EX/MEM payload into the predictor. Retain the existing EX\\nrepair connection and all external imem/dmem and channel-0 RVFI ports.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_branch_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for all source/tag and target bits, displacement\\nassociation, cold misses, overwrites by competing backedges, valid-only\\nreset, canceled pending writes, pre-edge lookup/write collisions, and\\nonce-per-accepted-owner training across holds. Verify full-address\\npage-crossing and wraparound cases without adding benchmark-specific PCs.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Verify zero-bubble warm backedges and one-slot loop-exit recovery,\\nnested-loop replacement, and stale hits after changing displacement,\\nopcode, condition, or registers. Include legal/misaligned JAL/JALR,\\nillegal instructions, ordinary ALU, loads/stores, and DIV/REM at a\\nformerly cached branch PC. Exercise load forwarding, long dmem holds,\\ndivider waits, imem unavailability, reset, and consecutive repairs.\\nCompare full RVFI against the unchanged ISS and separately monitor\\naccepted memory writes and divider launches for wrong-path effects.\\nAdd optional marker-window predictor event counts only in the unit\\ntest harness; preserve every existing correctness assertion.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_id_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Update input packing and check displacement certification, changed\\nbranch conditions, repair polarity, full metadata retention, invalid\\ncontrol clearing, and independent payload capture during squashes.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_ex_result_banks.py\", \"description\": \"Update ID/EX layout and default new prediction flags to no prediction\\nin existing tests. Add held and completing divide-owner cases with\\nuncertified predictions, retaining all current result-bank, forwarding,\\nmemory-address, reset, and exact arithmetic assertions.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 268.66, \"delta_pct\": -34.44, \"vs_baseline\": -5.01, \"fmax_mhz\": 115.85, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4312067, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5696, \"ff\": 2201, \"seeds\": [108.48, 116.96, 115.85], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"Implemented the single-entry backedge predictor as specified. Correctness gates pass, but the measured timing loss rejects the forecasted fitness gain: the unchanged local evaluator reports 115.85 MHz median and 268.66 iter/sec, versus the supplied winner's 184.06 MHz and 409.80 iter/sec. These are approximately 37.06% lower Fmax and 34.44% lower fitness. No acceptance decision or evaluator record was changed.\\n\\nThe RTL changes are confined to cores/bench/rtl:\\n\\n- Added branch_predictor.sv with one valid bit, 30 source bits, 30 target bits, and the complete 12-bit B displacement. Synthesis retains all 73 entry flops. Only validity resets; reset cancels a pending payload write. Miss outputs are zero. Lookup requires exact source equality and word alignment, uses full addresses, and has no update bypass.\\n- IF selects the raw lookup target versus full-width PC+4. Reset and existing EX repair have priority; normal advancement requires fetch acceptance. imem_addr still comes directly from the PC register. A prediction does not flush its own instruction.\\n- IF/ID carries the lookup-use bit and displacement snapshot. ID compares every B displacement bit against a current legal branch decode, preserving architectural branch_op and source-register fields. ID/EX carries prediction_used, certified_backedge, and branch_op[0] XOR certified_backedge as registered repair polarity. Invalid/flush controls are inert, holds retain all owner metadata, and independent payload capture remains intact.\\n- EX shares equality/signed-less-than/unsigned-less-than predicates between actual branch resolution and the decode-folded repair polarity. No prediction uses ordinary EX recovery; certified predictions repair only false outcomes to PC+4; stale predictions always repair to the current architectural next PC, including illegal encodings, alignment traps, memory operations, and DIV/REM. The exceptional actual-next-PC selection remains separate from the ordinary redirect and certified-exit selections. RVFI always carries the actual next PC.\\n- EX repair is qualified by valid and reset, with no new EX-accept/div_wait gate. The unchanged hazard priority retains held memory/divider owners and clears only the younger combinational slot when the owner advances. Trapped jumps still suppress link writes.\\n- A registered train_pending pulse is generated only for an accepted legal aligned taken negative-displacement conditional branch. It clears on every other clock, including holds. The following edge writes the existing EX/MEM pc, branch_target and instruction displacement. There is no additional training payload bank, resident-state feedback, or live EX/memory-ready write enable.\\n\\nNo architectural deviations were needed. The decoder, arithmetic/divider implementation, divider completion bank, retained WB forwarding, hazard priority, directly registered dmem address, and nret=1 external port set are unchanged. Test-only additions include dynamic instruction versions and optional marker-window counters; there are no hardware event counters, workload PC constants, address truncations, new prediction classes, or evaluator/formal-bound changes.\\n\\nValidation:\\n\\n- Requested verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv: PASS, no warnings.\\n- Unchanged RVFI channel-0 pattern gate: PASS.\\n- Unit suite: 10 pytest runners pass. Final XML aggregate: 153 cocotb cases pass; the optional CoreMark measurement is skipped in normal runs and was also run separately to completion. Both real and ALTOPS arithmetic/result-bank tests pass. The final pipeline-only rerun after adding reset coverage passes.\\n- Directed coverage includes all tag/target bits, all displacement comparison bits, page crossings and modulo-2^32 wraparound, pre-edge lookup/write collisions, valid-only reset and canceled pending writes, once-per-owner staged training across holds, nested eviction, and cold/warm/exit timing. Warm-loop branch-to-successor gaps are exactly [2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2] clocks.\\n- Full RVFI comparison against the unchanged ISS passes for changed displacements, all six branch conditions and changed registers, forwarded loaded operands, ALU/multiply, legal and misaligned loads/stores/JAL/JALR, illegal instructions, and DIV/REM replacements. Independent accepted bus request and divider launch checks catch wrong-path effects and duplication. Long memory holds, unavailable imem, consecutive repairs, completion holds, and reset of a hot entry plus a stale dividing owner pass.\\n- Local formal status: PASS on the first RTL attempt, 53 checks passed and 0 failed, including liveness, pc_fwd/pc_bwd, unique, ill, and cover. No counterexample and no formal fix/retry were needed. The exact unchanged run_all.sh/checks_si.cfg/wrapper_si.sv were run in an isolated scratch copy with RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=6. Actual divider arithmetic remains covered by real unit tests and cosim; formal-deep was not run because divider arithmetic was unchanged.\\n- Unchanged make cosim TARGET=bench: PASS, both selftest full-trace ISS comparison and CoreMark CRC validation.\\n- Unchanged make fpga TARGET=bench with NRET=1 and BENCH=fpga/core_bench_si.sv: all three seeds route successfully. An initial invocation selected Makefile's default two-channel synthesis wrapper and stopped before routing; rerunning with the existing declared single-channel wrapper resolved that setup mismatch without modifying the contract.\\n\\n| Seed | Routed Fmax (MHz) | Critical period (ns) | Logic / routing (ns) |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\\n| 1 | 108.48 | 9.218 | 4.17 / 5.05 |\\n| 2 | 116.96 | 8.550 | 3.59 / 4.96 |\\n| 3 | 115.85 | 8.632 | 4.15 / 4.48 |\\n\\nThe authoritative local evaluator reports 4,312,067 marker-window cycles, 10 iterations, 268.66 iter/sec, 5,696 LUT4 and 2,201 FF. All resource capacities pass; BRAM usage remains 4 and MULT36X36 usage remains 1. UART validation, EBREAK completion, bracket markers and oob=false pass. Relative to the supplied rounded baseline numbers, the inferred cycle reduction is approximately 3.99%; this comparison is inferred from 184.06 MHz / 409.80 iter/sec, not a newly measured baseline run.\\n\\nAll three routed seeds were inspected, including the existing forwarding/JALR/alignment paths displaced by routing. Each worst path passes through forwarding and low JALR target alignment, then repair/hold/squash logic, ending at an ID control RESET pin. Seed 1 begins at ID state; seeds 2 and 3 begin at retained MEM/WB instruction/register-address bits. The predictor tag-to-PC path remains present through eight mapped combinational cells including muxes and a packing passthrough. This is a structural depth count, not an isolated path-period measurement. PC data endpoints were also inspected in each detailed timing report.\\n\\nThe predictor payload CE cone was checked in every routed netlist: all 72 payload flops share a single LUT2 driven only by registered train_pending and reset. Validity is enabled directly by train_pending. There is no live EX comparator, resident match, or memory-ready input to those enables. Detailed reports contain the training-pulse D and validity-CE endpoint arrivals; the full payload-enable connectivity was checked separately. No claim is made that this wide physical net is free of routing cost.\\n\\nDetailed reporting required replaying the same three seeds with only --report and --detailed-timing-report added. All three reproduced the evaluator's routed Fmax exactly to its reported precision. A preliminary attempt to reload an already routed JSON for report-only analysis crashed inside the installed nextpnr array2d assertion; it did not affect the completed gate or its artifacts.\\n\\nOptional unit-harness CoreMark counters used the unchanged ELF and the exact C++ harness xorshift stall sequence. The measured start/stop cycles were 15,666 and 4,327,733, reproducing the evaluator's 4,312,067-cycle window exactly:\\n\\n| Marker-window event | Count |\\n| --- | ---: |\\n| Useful certified taken hits | 192,341 |\\n| Certified loop-exit repairs | 12,211 |\\n| Stale repairs | 0 |\\n| Ordinary repairs | 165,186 |\\n| Staged entry writes | 235,191 |\\n| Entry replacements (resident tuple changed) | 42,850 |\\n\\nThe live fixture discrepancy remains explicit: Makefile/evaluator defaults use TOTAL_DATA_SIZE=2000, -O3, ITERATIONS=10 and CRCs e714/1fd7/8e3a. The evaluator fitness above uses that unchanged fixture. A separately compiled TOTAL_DATA_SIZE=6000, -O3, ITERATIONS=10 ELF passed d4b0/be52/5e47, the literal validation message, EBREAK, OOB and marker checks. Its window is 55,554 to 31,597,703, or 31,542,149 cycles; 36.73 iter/sec at this candidate's median Fmax is a separate derived 6 KB measurement, not evaluator fitness. The UART compiler-flags string still says -O2 in both binaries; the captured actual compile commands use -O3.\\n\\nRemaining concern: small storage and staged writes did not preserve timing. The roughly 4% cycle improvement cannot offset the measured 37% median Fmax loss. This implementation is functionally validated but is not a fitness improvement over the supplied winner.\\n\\nValidation artifacts are preserved under /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/astra-max-20260905/bench-runs/gpt-6-astra_max-rep2/.tmp/r7s2-validation-_8mhz1xm. Relevant files are formal-gate.log, formal/last_run-15123.log, cosim-gate.log, fpga-gate.log, predictor-counts.json, predictor-measurement.log, sixkb-build.log, sixkb-coremark.log, timing-inspection.json, routed-cone-inspection.json, and cores/bench/generated/pnr_seed{1,2,3}/{nextpnr.log,timing.json,timing-full.log}. Unit logs are under $TMPDIR/r7s2-unit-tests-final.log and $TMPDIR/r7s2-pipeline-final.log. Scratch contract copies and generated outputs stay under $TMPDIR; no protected worktree files or other cores were changed.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-06T11:29:15.020506Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-06 hyp-20260906-003-r7s2 (regression, -34.44%): Registering train_pending isolated predictor payload enables from live EX qualification, but single-entry backedge prediction with decode displacement certification still left forwarding/JALR alignment through repair/hold/squash to ID control RESET critical in all three seeds, losing 37.06% median Fmax for an inferred ~4% CoreMark cycle saving.\"}\n25:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260906-003-r8s2\", \"title\": \"Backward-branch prediction with validity-only EX annul\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current core predicts sequentially and loses one useful fetch/decode\\nslot for each normally advancing taken control transfer. The branch-only\\nstatic predictor in r5s2 reduced evaluator cycles by 4.05%, but its repair\\nand hazard paths still reached the RESET pins of 24 ID/EX control, valid,\\nand prediction flops. Its median Fmax fell to 146.05 MHz. The single-entry\\npredictor in r7s2 similarly left forwarding/JALR alignment through repair\\nto ID control RESET critical and regressed fitness by 34.44%. Registered\\ntraining did not solve this recovery bottleneck. Moving recovery to MEM\\nin r6s2 failed the unchanged liveness check. These results favor retaining\\nEX recovery while reducing its ID/EX destination to one validity bit.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current core predicts sequentially and loses one useful fetch/decode\\nslot for each normally advancing taken control transfer. The branch-only\\nstatic predictor in r5s2 reduced evaluator cycles by 4.05%, but its repair\\nand hazard paths still reached the RESET pins of 24 ID/EX control, valid,\\nand prediction flops. Its median Fmax fell to 146.05 MHz. The single-entry\\npredictor in r7s2 similarly left forwarding/JALR alignment through repair\\nto ID control RESET critical and regressed fitness by 34.44%. Registered\\ntraining did not solve this recovery bottleneck. Moving recovery to MEM\\nin r6s2 failed the unchanged liveness check. These results favor retaining\\nEX recovery while reducing its ID/EX destination to one validity bit.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Implement one static backward-taken conditional-branch predictor whose\\nEX recovery annuls the younger slot solely through its registered valid\\nbit. The new architectural claim is that validity-qualified consumers\\ncan make the previously measured branch-cycle saving profitable by\\nremoving repair from the entire ID/EX decode-control bank as well as\\nits data payload. Retain the existing pipeline depth and one-slot EX\\nrepair penalty. Use the branch-only policy from r5s2 to isolate this\\nchange in predictor recovery; JAL/JALR remain sequentially predicted.\\n\\nIF predecodes raw imem_data for opcode 0x63 and legal funct3 values\\n0, 1, 4, 5, 6, and 7. Predict taken only for a negative B displacement\\n(instruction bit 31), word-aligned fetch PC, and instruction bit 8 clear.\\nConstruct the sign-extended B displacement and add it to the full PC;\\npreserve all 32 address bits and modulo-2^32 carry behavior. Compute\\nPC+4 independently. Select between these values using raw eligibility,\\nindependent of stall, flush, redirect, and acceptance qualification.\\nUpdate the PC only on the existing accepted fetch edge, with reset and\\nEX repair taking priority. Keep imem_addr directly driven by the PC\\nregister. There is no table, training, saved target, or additional stage.\\n\\nCarry predicted_taken with the exact raw instruction used to choose\\nthe fetch next PC. IF always exposes raw instruction and prediction\\nbits; flush and instruction unavailability affect validity only.\\nRemove the redirect-driven NOP mux so repair cannot reach the decoded\\ncontrol D inputs through instruction masking. In ID, keep architectural\\nbranch_op unchanged and register repair_invert = branch_op[0] XOR\\npredicted_taken. Register branch_repair_enable for a decoded legal\\nbranch with an aligned target, using only the two-bit sum of PC and\\nimmediate low bits. These three metadata bits use ordinary payload\\ncapture and hold rules and are meaningful only when ID/EX is valid.\\n\\nMake ID/EX valid the sole dynamically squashed ID/EX field. Its existing\\nreset, flush, and stall priority remains: an eligible flush clears valid,\\nan ordinary capture takes fetch validity, and a memory/divider hold\\nretains the current owner. The complete ctrl_t, prediction metadata,\\nand existing instruction/data fields have synchronous reset and the\\nordinary !stall capture enable only. Capture raw decoded controls on\\nan advancing edge even when fetch is invalid or a repair discards it.\\nA load-use flush clears valid while its ordinary stall retains payload.\\nDo not zero or mask the control bank with flush or fetch validity, and\\ndo not mask the ID/EX output bundle with valid. Invalid raw controls\\nare intentionally unspecified as instructions but remain defined bits.\\n\\nQualify every action that can consume these raw ID/EX controls with\\nthe registered owner validity. Specifically, pass ID/EX valid into\\nhazard_unit and compute load_use_hazard from valid AND mem_read before\\ncomparing rd with the raw fetched register addresses. Do not gate this\\ncomparison with repair-dependent fetch validity or masked instructions;\\nthe current valid branch/jump cannot simultaneously be an EX load.\\nKeep EX redirect and divider request/wait/accept qualified by in.valid;\\naudit that no invalid opcode can stall, redirect, or launch arithmetic.\\nPreserve EX/MEM's existing control-zero bubble conversion whenever\\n!in.valid or div_wait. Thus downstream forwarding producers and memory\\nrequests still see zero controls for invalid EX/MEM entries. Preserve\\nretained MEM/WB forwarding data during dmem holds, including valid=0\\nretention after retirement; do not add a MEM/WB-valid forwarding gate.\\n\\nEX shares forwarded equality, signed-less-than, and unsigned-less-than\\npredicates. Select base_cond with architectural branch_op[2:1]; use\\noriginal branch_op[0] for architectural direction and the registered\\nrepair_invert for direction mismatch. Branch repair is in.valid AND\\nbranch_repair_enable AND (base_cond XOR repair_invert). Combine it with\\nthe current valid, legal, aligned JAL/JALR redirect contribution.\\nA predicted branch exit repairs to PC+4; an unpredicted taken branch\\nrepairs to its branch target. Select the branch repair target from\\nregistered predicted_taken, independently of the live comparison.\\nCorrect predictions preserve the useful younger instruction without\\na bubble. Keep taken-only alignment traps, JALR bit-zero clearing,\\nlink-write suppression on traps, and actual resolved RVFI pc_next.\\n\\nPreserve the current EX redirect priority over imem backpressure and\\nthe current hold priority for an owner blocked by dmem. A held branch\\ncan keep asserting its repair until advancement; it must retain its\\ncomplete instruction and prediction metadata. When it advances, only\\nthe younger combinational fetch slot is annulled. Do not add div_wait\\nor a generic EX-accept qualifier to the branch recovery cone. Recovery\\nremains in EX and cannot let a wrong-path instruction reach a memory\\nowner, retire, or launch DIV/REM. No extra recovery cycle is permitted.\\n\\nThis tests a different recovery boundary from r5s2's control-bank\\nsquashes: the repair-to-ID cone should terminate only at the valid\\nflop, with no path to decode-control, prediction-metadata, or payload\\nRESET, CE, or D pins. PC repair remains required. Inspect the mapped\\nfanout and all three routed seeds to verify this physical claim;\\nsource-level separation alone is insufficient. Also inspect the new\\nvalid-qualified hazard path and the instruction-to-PC target adder.\\nThey may become critical even after the control-reset paths disappear.\\n\\nEstimate a 3% net fitness improvement with low confidence. Repeating\\nthe prior 4.05% cycle reduction requires about 176.61 MHz to break even\\nagainst the supplied 184.06 MHz, 409.80 iter/sec winner. A 1% Fmax loss\\nwith that cycle reduction would yield about 3.18% greater fitness.\\nThese are conditional estimates, not measured results. Measure actual\\nmarker-window cycles and median routed Fmax; do not accept cycle savings\\nalone. Run unchanged lint, unit, formal including liveness, ISS cosim,\\nCRC/UART, OOB, marker, resource, and three-seed FPGA checks. Compare\\nidentical workload builds and disclose the actual evaluator workload\\nif it differs from the prompt; do not change the evaluation contract.\\nPreserve nret=1, all hard invariants, arithmetic/result-bank ownership,\\nand the directly registered dmem address. Scope is cores/bench only.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted_taken to if_id_t and the prediction, folded repair\\npolarity, and aligned-branch repair-enable bits to id_ex_t. Document\\nthat ID/EX valid owns all actions even when raw controls are nonzero.\\nKeep EX/MEM control-zero bubbles and the RVFI bundle contract intact.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement the specified aligned backward-branch predecode and full\\ntarget adder. Expose raw instruction/prediction bits without a flush\\nNOP mux, using validity for unavailable or discarded fetches. Keep\\nraw target selection separate from PC acceptance, preserve repair\\npriority, and retain directly registered instruction addressing.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Move decoded controls and prediction metadata into the ordinary\\npayload capture/hold domain. Dynamic flush and invalid fetches alter\\nonly registered validity. Preserve full synchronous reset, exact\\nheld-owner association, decoder legality, and operand capture.\\nRemove both repair-driven control clears and validity-driven control\\ninput masks; do not reintroduce a whole-bundle output mask.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the ID/EX owner-valid input and qualify the EX load-use producer\\nwith it. Keep raw fetched register-address comparisons independent\\nof redirect and fetch-valid masking. Preserve load-use bubbling,\\nmemory/divider holds, fetch backpressure, and repair priorities.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire registered ID/EX validity into load-use detection and update\\npredictor/recovery interface connections and comments as needed.\\nAudit every ID/EX control consumer under the new invalid-payload\\nrepresentation. Preserve all top-level imem/dmem and channel-0 RVFI\\nports, downstream forwarding wiring, and direct memory-address bank.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use registered repair polarity with the shared branch predicates\\nfor one-slot EX recovery. Keep architectural direction, next PC,\\ntraps, jump links, and forwarded operands unchanged. Ensure invalid\\nraw controls cannot redirect, hold the divider, request or accept a\\ndivide, or produce active EX/MEM controls. Retain existing control-zero\\ndownstream bubbles, result-bank ownership, and memory-hold behavior.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add standalone fetch tests for all branch funct3 encodings, immediate\\nsigns and alignment bits, address carry/wrap, raw invalid instruction\\nexposure, changing stalled instruction data, prediction acceptance,\\nreset, and repair priority. Verify all non-branch opcodes remain\\nsequentially predicted and predictions do not invalidate themselves.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_id_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Update bundle packing and representation-dependent tests for a sole\\nvalidity squash. Check complete held-owner retention, raw control\\nand prediction capture despite flush, load-use annul with payload\\nhold, synchronous reset, and correct folded polarity/alignment.\\nPreserve decoder-legality and instruction-association assertions.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_ex_result_banks.py\", \"description\": \"Update ID/EX packing with prediction defaults disabled. Exercise\\ninvalid ID/EX entries carrying nonzero load, store, jump, and DIV/REM\\ncontrols: they must produce no redirect/divider action and only\\ncontrol-zero EX/MEM bubbles. Retain all result-bank, exact arithmetic,\\nforwarding-retention, completion, and memory-address assertions.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Compare full RVFI streams with the unchanged ISS for all branch\\nconditions/outcomes, warm backward loops and exits, forward branches,\\nlegal/misaligned jumps, illegal instructions, load dependencies,\\nimem unavailability, dmem holds, and divider waits. Check exactly\\nzero extra slots on correct prediction and one on EX repair without\\nstalls. Put loads, stores, branches, jumps, and divides in annulled\\nslots; independently assert no invalid load hazard, divider launch,\\naccepted memory side effect, forwarding producer, or retirement.\\nReplace only raw-ID-control-zero representation assertions with\\nvalidity-qualified behavior checks, preserving every architectural\\nassertion and control-zero invalid EX/MEM check. Include consecutive\\nrepairs and reset during a held owner; retain RVFI order/PC checks.\\n\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted_taken to if_id_t and the prediction, folded repair\\npolarity, and aligned-branch repair-enable bits to id_ex_t. Document\\nthat ID/EX valid owns all actions even when raw controls are nonzero.\\nKeep EX/MEM control-zero bubbles and the RVFI bundle contract intact.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement the specified aligned backward-branch predecode and full\\ntarget adder. Expose raw instruction/prediction bits without a flush\\nNOP mux, using validity for unavailable or discarded fetches. Keep\\nraw target selection separate from PC acceptance, preserve repair\\npriority, and retain directly registered instruction addressing.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Move decoded controls and prediction metadata into the ordinary\\npayload capture/hold domain. Dynamic flush and invalid fetches alter\\nonly registered validity. Preserve full synchronous reset, exact\\nheld-owner association, decoder legality, and operand capture.\\nRemove both repair-driven control clears and validity-driven control\\ninput masks; do not reintroduce a whole-bundle output mask.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the ID/EX owner-valid input and qualify the EX load-use producer\\nwith it. Keep raw fetched register-address comparisons independent\\nof redirect and fetch-valid masking. Preserve load-use bubbling,\\nmemory/divider holds, fetch backpressure, and repair priorities.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire registered ID/EX validity into load-use detection and update\\npredictor/recovery interface connections and comments as needed.\\nAudit every ID/EX control consumer under the new invalid-payload\\nrepresentation. Preserve all top-level imem/dmem and channel-0 RVFI\\nports, downstream forwarding wiring, and direct memory-address bank.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use registered repair polarity with the shared branch predicates\\nfor one-slot EX recovery. Keep architectural direction, next PC,\\ntraps, jump links, and forwarded operands unchanged. Ensure invalid\\nraw controls cannot redirect, hold the divider, request or accept a\\ndivide, or produce active EX/MEM controls. Retain existing control-zero\\ndownstream bubbles, result-bank ownership, and memory-hold behavior.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add standalone fetch tests for all branch funct3 encodings, immediate\\nsigns and alignment bits, address carry/wrap, raw invalid instruction\\nexposure, changing stalled instruction data, prediction acceptance,\\nreset, and repair priority. Verify all non-branch opcodes remain\\nsequentially predicted and predictions do not invalidate themselves.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_id_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Update bundle packing and representation-dependent tests for a sole\\nvalidity squash. Check complete held-owner retention, raw control\\nand prediction capture despite flush, load-use annul with payload\\nhold, synchronous reset, and correct folded polarity/alignment.\\nPreserve decoder-legality and instruction-association assertions.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_ex_result_banks.py\", \"description\": \"Update ID/EX packing with prediction defaults disabled. Exercise\\ninvalid ID/EX entries carrying nonzero load, store, jump, and DIV/REM\\ncontrols: they must produce no redirect/divider action and only\\ncontrol-zero EX/MEM bubbles. Retain all result-bank, exact arithmetic,\\nforwarding-retention, completion, and memory-address assertions.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Compare full RVFI streams with the unchanged ISS for all branch\\nconditions/outcomes, warm backward loops and exits, forward branches,\\nlegal/misaligned jumps, illegal instructions, load dependencies,\\nimem unavailability, dmem holds, and divider waits. Check exactly\\nzero extra slots on correct prediction and one on EX repair without\\nstalls. Put loads, stores, branches, jumps, and divides in annulled\\nslots; independently assert no invalid load hazard, divider launch,\\naccepted memory side effect, forwarding producer, or retirement.\\nReplace only raw-ID-control-zero representation assertions with\\nvalidity-qualified behavior checks, preserving every architectural\\nassertion and control-zero invalid EX/MEM check. Include consecutive\\nrepairs and reset during a held owner; retain RVFI order/PC checks.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 206.45, \"delta_pct\": -49.62, \"vs_baseline\": -27.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 88.97, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4309463, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5578, \"ff\": 2095, \"seeds\": [90.53, 88.97, 87.28], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-06T12:07:20.285691Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-06 hyp-20260906-003-r8s2 (regression, -49.62%): Validity-only ID/EX annul isolated repair from the control/payload bank, but forwarding through 27-31 carry arcs to the remaining valid RESET still limited all three routed seeds, dropping median Fmax from 184.06 to 88.97 MHz despite 4.05% fewer CoreMark cycles; reducing squash fanout alone does not shorten recovery logic.\"}\n26:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260906-001-r9s0\", \"title\": \"Flatten EX operand selection with direct one-hot forwarding\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The accepted r5s1 implementation reaches 409.80 fitness at a reported\\nmedian 184.06 MHz. Its seed-1 and seed-3 limiting paths run from EX/MEM\\ndestination tags through forwarding selection and JALR resolution to\\nIF PC bit 1. The current forward_unit encodes a priority decision into\\ntwo bits, ex_stage decodes those bits to select each raw operand, and\\nALU inputs then pass through separate PC/immediate selection muxes.\\nThis is a small combinational network on several important EX paths.\\n\\nPrior micro_opt experiments include unsuccessful register-file one-hot\\nreads (r5s0), JALR alignment precomputation (r6s0), and ALU operation\\nrecoding (r7s0). The structural forwarding-retiming experiment r6s1\\nretained the encoded 00/01/10 forwarding interface and regressed 8.01%.\\nNone tested direct mutually exclusive forwarding controls combined\\nwith flattened ALU input selection. Their timing regressions also show\\nthat local gate reduction alone cannot establish a fitness benefit.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The accepted r5s1 implementation reaches 409.80 fitness at a reported\\nmedian 184.06 MHz. Its seed-1 and seed-3 limiting paths run from EX/MEM\\ndestination tags through forwarding selection and JALR resolution to\\nIF PC bit 1. The current forward_unit encodes a priority decision into\\ntwo bits, ex_stage decodes those bits to select each raw operand, and\\nALU inputs then pass through separate PC/immediate selection muxes.\\nThis is a small combinational network on several important EX paths.\\n\\nPrior micro_opt experiments include unsuccessful register-file one-hot\\nreads (r5s0), JALR alignment precomputation (r6s0), and ALU operation\\nrecoding (r7s0). The structural forwarding-retiming experiment r6s1\\nretained the encoded 00/01/10 forwarding interface and regressed 8.01%.\\nNone tested direct mutually exclusive forwarding controls combined\\nwith flattened ALU input selection. Their timing regressions also show\\nthat local gate reduction alone cannot establish a fitness benefit.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the encoded forwarding-selection network with direct one-hot\\nsource enables and use those enables to flatten EX operand selection.\\nThis is one combinational micro-optimization: no new state, pipeline\\nboundary, arithmetic operation, predictor, or forwarding source.\\n\\nFor each raw source register, compute the existing live EX/MEM and\\nMEM/WB matches in parallel:\\n  E = ex_mem_w_en && ex_mem_rd != 0 && ex_mem_rd == source;\\n  W = mem_wb_w_en && mem_wb_rd != 0 && mem_wb_rd == source.\\nEmit a three-bit vector with bit 0 = !(E || W), bit 1 = E, and\\nbit 2 = !E && W. Thus exactly one of the captured ID operand, EX/MEM\\nresult, and MEM/WB writeback data is selected, preserving youngest\\neligible writer priority. Remove the two-bit encode/decode interface\\nthroughout the core; do not generate the new enables by decoding the\\nold selectors. Keep comparisons combinational at their current stage.\\n\\nForm each raw forwarded rs value as the OR of its three masked data\\ncandidates. Independently form alu_a from four mutually exclusive\\nterms: the same three candidates with their enables qualified by\\n!in.ctrl.is_auipc, plus in.pc qualified by in.ctrl.is_auipc. Form alu_b\\nanalogously using !in.ctrl.alu_src for the three register candidates\\nand in.imm qualified by in.ctrl.alu_src. Express the four-term merges\\nas balanced pairwise ORs. In particular, do not implement the ALU\\ninputs by putting a PC/immediate mux after the raw forwarded bus.\\nAll data and control values remain fully defined, including bubbles;\\ndo not add synthesis don't-cares or technology-specific primitives.\\n\\nBranch comparison, full-width JALR addition, store data, raw RVFI\\noperands, and saved divider operands must still use the unmodified\\nsemantic raw rs1/rs2 selections. Keep the ALU operation encoding,\\nresult-selection case, multiplier expressions and sharing, division\\narithmetic, ALTOPS formulas, and all result-bank ownership unchanged.\\nUpdate div_operands_ready to test the EX/MEM enable bit directly for\\neither source, retaining its current load-address exclusion only at\\ndivider launch. Do not globally exclude loads from forwarding or\\nalter the existing load-use interlock and raw-operand RVFI contract.\\n\\nPreserve the original forwarding producer qualifications. In\\nparticular, use MEM/WB ctrl.reg_write rather than retirement valid or\\nwb_w_en: an already-retired writer's retained data must still forward\\nduring a dmem hold. Keep trap-suppressed writers ineligible, x0\\nprotected, and all existing reset, flush, redirect, memory-hold, and\\ndivider-wait priorities. The direct normal EX/MEM memory-address bank,\\ncontrol-zero bubbles, nret=1 ports, and retirement timing are unchanged.\\n\\nThe physical hypothesis is that direct enables remove redundant\\npriority encoding/decoding on raw forwarding and avoid a serial mux\\nlevel on the ALU inputs, shortening tag-to-JALR and tag-to-ALU paths.\\nSynthesis may already simplify some of the old encoding, and added\\nenable fanout or different placement may outweigh the reduction.\\nInspect the mapped cones and all three routed seeds, including the\\ncompeting ALU-result-selection and register-file paths. Preserve one\\nMULT36X36 and the existing four memory BSRAMs. Missing timing arcs are\\nunknown delays, not evidence of margin; do not modify timing models.\\n\\nPredict unchanged CoreMark marker-window cycles and a modest 3% median\\nFmax/fitness gain, approximately 422.09 fitness if the supplied winner's\\nworkload and cycle count are reproduced. This is an unmeasured estimate\\nwith low confidence. Require unchanged architectural RVFI streams and\\nretirement-cycle sequences under identical bus schedules, then use the\\nexisting lint, unit, formal including liveness, ISS cosim, and three-seed\\nFPGA gates. Keep all CRC, UART, address-bound, and timing-marker checks.\\nPrior notes distinguish the evaluator's 2 KB workload from supplemental\\n6 KB runs; disclose the actual measured build and verify the requested\\ncanonical 6 KB workload separately if needed, without changing the\\nevaluation contract or comparing different binaries across variants.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace both encoded two-bit outputs with direct three-bit one-hot\\nsource enables derived from the existing live tag matches. Preserve\\nnonzero destination checks, EX/MEM priority, and retained MEM/WB\\neligibility. Add no registers, valid qualification, or stall gating.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect the new forwarding vectors directly between forward_unit\\nand ex_stage and update their declarations and comments. Preserve\\nall top-level ports, producer write-enable connections, hazards,\\nresult-bank connections, and directly registered memory addressing.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume one-hot enables with masked-OR raw operand selection and\\nindependent four-candidate ALU input merges that include PC or\\nimmediate selection in the masks. Remove the encoded case muxes\\nand serial ALU source muxes. Use the EX/MEM enable bit for the\\nexisting divider operand-readiness check. Preserve arithmetic,\\nraw-operand consumers, metadata, pipeline registers, and controls.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_forward_unit.py\", \"description\": \"Add a cocotb suite and runner in this permitted test file. Check\\nboth ports across all source/destination tag combinations and\\nproducer-enable combinations, including x0 and competing writers.\\nAssert exactly one source is selected and that it is the freshest\\neligible architectural writer; exercise independently differing\\nsource ports and immediate combinational changes without a clock.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_ex_result_banks.py\", \"description\": \"Adapt stimulus to the new internal selector representation without\\nweakening existing assertions. Exercise all nine legal source-pair\\nselections with distinct data, independent PC/immediate overrides,\\nand real/ALTOPS modes. Check raw RVFI/store/branch operands remain\\nseparate from ALU overrides; retain exact divider latency, load\\nreadiness, saved operands, result-bank ownership, holds, and reset.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed ALU, immediate, AUIPC, branch, JALR, store, and DIV/REM\\nconsumers with each producer distance, simultaneous matching\\nwriters, x0, true load-use dependencies, and trap-suppressed writes.\\nInclude long dmem holds retaining a valid-cleared MEM/WB source,\\noverlapping imem stalls, and consecutive dependent divides.\\nCompare full RVFI and accepted memory effects against the unchanged\\nISS and verify baseline-equivalent retirement-cycle sequences for\\nidentical instruction and bus schedules. Keep all existing checks.\\n\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace both encoded two-bit outputs with direct three-bit one-hot\\nsource enables derived from the existing live tag matches. Preserve\\nnonzero destination checks, EX/MEM priority, and retained MEM/WB\\neligibility. Add no registers, valid qualification, or stall gating.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect the new forwarding vectors directly between forward_unit\\nand ex_stage and update their declarations and comments. Preserve\\nall top-level ports, producer write-enable connections, hazards,\\nresult-bank connections, and directly registered memory addressing.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume one-hot enables with masked-OR raw operand selection and\\nindependent four-candidate ALU input merges that include PC or\\nimmediate selection in the masks. Remove the encoded case muxes\\nand serial ALU source muxes. Use the EX/MEM enable bit for the\\nexisting divider operand-readiness check. Preserve arithmetic,\\nraw-operand consumers, metadata, pipeline registers, and controls.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_forward_unit.py\", \"description\": \"Add a cocotb suite and runner in this permitted test file. Check\\nboth ports across all source/destination tag combinations and\\nproducer-enable combinations, including x0 and competing writers.\\nAssert exactly one source is selected and that it is the freshest\\neligible architectural writer; exercise independently differing\\nsource ports and immediate combinational changes without a clock.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_ex_result_banks.py\", \"description\": \"Adapt stimulus to the new internal selector representation without\\nweakening existing assertions. Exercise all nine legal source-pair\\nselections with distinct data, independent PC/immediate overrides,\\nand real/ALTOPS modes. Check raw RVFI/store/branch operands remain\\nseparate from ALU overrides; retain exact divider latency, load\\nreadiness, saved operands, result-bank ownership, holds, and reset.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed ALU, immediate, AUIPC, branch, JALR, store, and DIV/REM\\nconsumers with each producer distance, simultaneous matching\\nwriters, x0, true load-use dependencies, and trap-suppressed writes.\\nInclude long dmem holds retaining a valid-cleared MEM/WB source,\\noverlapping imem stalls, and consecutive dependent divides.\\nCompare full RVFI and accepted memory effects against the unchanged\\nISS and verify baseline-equivalent retirement-cycle sequences for\\nidentical instruction and bus schedules. Keep all existing checks.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 392.74, \"delta_pct\": -4.16, \"vs_baseline\": 38.87, \"fmax_mhz\": 176.4, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5531, \"ff\": 2091, \"seeds\": [173.07, 176.4, 187.97], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"# Flatten EX operand selection with direct one-hot forwarding\\n\\nImplemented the requested combinational change. Local correctness gates pass,\\nbut the physical hypothesis regresses: median Fmax is 176.40 MHz and fitness\\n392.74, versus the reproduced baseline's 184.06 MHz and 409.80 (-4.16%).\\nThe predicted 3% improvement was not observed. The implementation is left\\nfor the orchestrator to evaluate; local correctness does not imply acceptance.\\n\\n## Implementation\\n\\n- Only `cores/bench/rtl/{forward_unit,core,ex_stage}.sv` changed in RTL.\\n- `forward_unit` computes live EX/MEM and MEM/WB tag matches independently\\n  and directly emits `{!E && W, E, !(E || W)}` for each source. The two-bit\\n  forwarding interface is removed. EX/MEM wins competing matches; x0 is\\n  excluded through the existing nonzero producer checks.\\n- `core` connects three-bit `fwd_rs1_en` / `fwd_rs2_en`. Both producer\\n  qualifications remain `ctrl.reg_write`, including retained, valid-cleared\\n  MEM/WB writers during dmem holds. No valid, writeback-enable, load, or\\n  stall qualification was added to the forwarding matches.\\n- `ex_stage` uses three masked candidates for each semantic raw operand.\\n  ALU inputs independently merge four masked candidates with balanced\\n  pairwise ORs, qualifying the register terms with !is_auipc / !alu_src\\n  and the PC / immediate terms with the corresponding positive controls.\\n  No RTL mux follows the raw forwarded bus to select the ALU input.\\n- Divider launch readiness directly tests enable bit 1 on either port.\\n  The load-address exclusion remains confined to divider launch.\\n- Branch comparisons, full-width JALR addition, stores, RVFI and saved\\n  divider operands still consume raw rs1/rs2. Arithmetic, ALTOPS formulas,\\n  ALU operation/result cases, result-bank ownership, direct memory-address\\n  register, reset/hold/flush priorities and all top-level nret=1 ports are\\n  unchanged. No registers, don't-cares or technology primitives were added.\\n\\n## Tests and equivalence\\n\\n- Added `test_forward_unit.py`: all 4,194,304 combinations of both source\\n  tags, both destination tags and both producer enables, plus immediate\\n  combinational transitions without a clock. Checks exactly-one selection,\\n  independently different source ports, x0 and youngest-writer priority.\\n- Adapted `test_ex_result_banks.py` to one-hot controls without removing\\n  assertions. Added all nine source pairs with independent PC/immediate\\n  overrides, ADD/MUL in real and ALTOPS modes, every branch comparison,\\n  full-width JALR carry/alignment cases, raw store/RVFI operands, and all\\n  four DIV/REM operations with load readiness and saved forwarded operands.\\n  Existing exact latency, held completion, result ownership, reset and\\n  inactive-payload checks remain active.\\n- Extended `test_pipeline.py` with producer distances, competing writers,\\n  ALU/immediate/AUIPC/branch/JALR/store/DIV/REM consumers, x0, real load-use\\n  dependencies, trap-suppressed writes, consecutive dependent divisions,\\n  and 17-cycle dmem holds with overlapping imem stalls and retained WB data.\\n- All 10 candidate pytest runners passed: 149 cocotb tests across real\\n  arithmetic, ALTOPS and pipeline configurations. The unchanged baseline\\n  additionally passed the same 25 pipeline tests.\\n- Optional `PIPELINE_TRACE_DIR` / `PIPELINE_TRACE_MODE=record` records a\\n  baseline run; other modes compare. Baseline RTL was copied before edits\\n  and selected through the existing test helper's RTL/build paths. Exact\\n  comparison passed for 50 distinct bus schedules, 6,503 retirements,\\n  1,599 accepted memory effects and 29,990 driven cycles. Every RVFI field,\\n  retirement cycle, accepted memory cycle/data, final memory and driven\\n  ready schedule matched. The existing unchanged Python ISS checks also\\n  passed for these programs.\\n\\n## Local gates\\n\\n- Requested Verilator lint command: PASS, no warnings/errors.\\n- Local formal: **PASS, 53 passed / 0 failed**, including liveness, unique,\\n  cover and channel-0 checks. Used unchanged `formal/run_all.sh`, automatic\\n  nret=1 selection, `checks_si.cfg`, `wrapper_si.sv` and bitwuzla, JOBS=4.\\n  The complete run took about 63 seconds; no RTL fix attempts or formal\\n  counterexamples. An initial invocation exited before generating checks\\n  because the default Python lacked PyYAML. Selecting the installed\\n  Miniconda Python environment resolved this prerequisite issue.\\n- Existing `tools.eval.cosim.run_cosim`: PASS, selftest and evaluator\\n  CoreMark ELF. No ISS/harness/evaluation files were edited.\\n- Unchanged synthesis and FPGA evaluation scripts: all three routed seeds\\n  completed successfully. Baseline seeds were independently rerun and\\n  exactly reproduced the supplied winner.\\n- `formal-deep` was not run: arithmetic is unchanged; real arithmetic was\\n  exercised by unit tests, directed ISS checks and both CoreMark workloads.\\n\\n## Routed results and mapped cones\\n\\n| Variant | Seed 1 MHz | Seed 2 MHz | Seed 3 MHz | Median MHz | Fitness | LUT4 | DFF | MULT36X36 | BSRAM |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\n| Original snapshot | 184.06 | 191.13 | 179.89 | 184.06 | 409.80 | 5490 | 2112 | 1 | 4 |\\n| Direct enables | 173.07 | 176.40 | 187.97 | 176.40 | 392.74 | 5531 | 2091 | 1 | 4 |\\n\\nThe synthesized four memory cells remain DPX9B. The 21 fewer mapped DFFs\\nresult from synthesis optimization; RTL state/ownership is unchanged.\\n\\nBoth mapped designs still use 32 final LUT3 cells on each ALU operand,\\nwith mux INIT=0xB8; bit-0 cones retain a MUX2_LUT5 and LUT3 feeding that\\nfinal mux. Direct RTL enables did not force a flat physical mux. The\\nlongest structural tag-to-ALU-input path remains five LUT/MUX cells for\\nboth operands. Graph traversal also retains the long ALU arithmetic and\\nresult-selection cone, and the seven-cell RF-to-ID read cone. Structural\\ncounts include primitive dependencies and are not timing measurements.\\n\\nBaseline seeds 1/3 are limited by EX/MEM rd[0] through forwarding/JALR to\\nIF PC[1], at 5.43/5.56 ns. Baseline seed 2 is limited by wrapper LFSR[20]\\nthrough fetch/register-read selection into ID, at 5.23 ns.\\n\\nCandidate seed 1 is limited by RF x14[3] to ID at 5.78 ns (2.49 ns logic,\\n3.29 ns routing). Seeds 2/3 are limited by wrapper LFSR[20] through the\\nfetch/register-read cone into ID at 5.67/5.32 ns (2.50/2.39 ns logic and\\n3.17/2.93 ns routing). Thus moving the original limiting cone did not\\nimprove the median timing result.\\n\\nAdditional detailed-report routes reproduced the same three candidate\\nfrequencies. Inspected the normal ALU-result register endpoints as well:\\nbits 2 and 11 have the largest native detailed-delay entries in seeds\\n1/2, and bit 5 in seed 3. Reports contain only 11 normal-result bits and\\none IF PC bit; unreported paths and missing technology arcs are unknown,\\nnot evidence of timing margin. Native detailed-delay fields are kept\\nseparate from the authoritative final Fmax/critical-path reports. Timing\\nmodels and constraints were not modified. A readback-only attempt to\\nanalyze saved PNR JSON crashed in nextpnr's array2d assertion; generating\\nreports by routing the original synth JSON succeeded reproducibly.\\n\\n## Workload disclosure\\n\\nThe evaluator actually uses TOTAL_DATA_SIZE=2000, ITERATIONS=10, -O3 and\\n`--bench --istall --dstall`. That binary reproduced the winner's\\n**4,491,485 marker-window cycles** (start 15,801; stop 4,507,286). Its UART\\npassed the existing validator: seedcrc=e9f5, list=e714, matrix=1fd7,\\nstate=8e3a, final=fcaf and `Correct operation validated.` No OOB access.\\nThis 2 KB result alone determines the fitness above.\\n\\nSeparately built the requested TOTAL_DATA_SIZE=6000, ITERATIONS=10, -O3\\nbinary in scratch and ran it on both variants with identical bus seeds.\\nBoth gave **32,836,671 marker-window cycles** (start 56,393; stop\\n32,893,064), seedcrc=8a02, list=d4b0, matrix=be52, state=5e47,\\nfinal=5949, validation literal present, clean EBREAK and no OOB access.\\nThe 6 KB binary is not substituted into the evaluator or compared against\\nthe 2 KB binary. The UART's hardcoded compiler-flags string still says\\n`-O2 -march=rv32im`; the actual logged build commands use -O3 for both.\\nCoreMark's printed size is per algorithm: 666 for 2 KB and 2000 for 6 KB.\\n\\nComplete non-bench RVFI output, including every retirement cycle, was\\nalso streamed and compared by byte count, retirement count and SHA-256\\nbetween baseline and candidate for each identical ELF:\\n\\n| Workload | Retirements | Final retirement cycle | RVFI bytes | Matching trace SHA-256 |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\\n| 2 KB | 2,937,037 | 4,514,348 | 854,161,634 | d7f581697e844a6001a0b1811d7b3df5e76a0c05a74ab3d5a5dad67b0460be36 |\\n| 6 KB | 22,093,920 | 32,900,232 | 6,463,986,468 | 34ef03d244b986a66be40660efea1b01b6705ecbf1263bf493d109b7184ac4a0 |\\n\\nELF SHA-256: 2 KB `0c13cb0f38ebe9ab87e2f70049e3a0e6dd9ab77b95b612d861951ccc2125361c`;\\n6 KB `da20d2553fa7fa0237d3ad52dcf40be9444bcaf0e53084e9d302331ada8f30b4`.\\n\\n## Scope and evidence\\n\\nNo implementation deviations from the hypothesis. Temporary copies,\\nbuilds, formal staging, PNR outputs and trace summaries live exclusively\\nunder `$TMPDIR/forwarding-r9s0/`; contract files were read or copied\\nunchanged. Notes are at the explicitly requested worktree-root path.\\n\\nEvidence under that scratch directory includes `mapped-cones.json`,\\n`physical-summary.json`, `routed-endpoint-review.json`,\\n`coremark-full-trace-equivalence.json`, `pipeline-traces/`,\\n`validation/{fpga-result,cosim-result,coremark-2k,coremark-6k}.json`,\\n`validation/formal/last_run-30236.log`, the unit/baseline/candidate test\\nXMLs, and each variant's `cores/bench/generated/pnr_seed*/` reports.\\nThe full CoreMark streams were hashed while streaming, not retained.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-06T12:49:00.636167Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-06 hyp-20260906-001-r9s0 (regression, -4.16%): Direct one-hot forwarding and balanced masked-OR ALU inputs in ex_stage.sv do not guarantee shallower mapping: synthesis retained final operand muxes and five-cell tag-to-ALU depth, while routing-dominated register-read paths became critical in all three seeds, reducing median Fmax 4.16% with unchanged CoreMark cycles.\"}\n27:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260906-002-r9s1\", \"title\": \"Register JALR targets in a two-cycle execute path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The accepted r5s1 design reaches 409.80 fitness at 184.06 MHz. Its saved\\nrouted reports identify EX/MEM destination-tag comparison, operand\\nforwarding, and JALR target generation into the IF PC as the limiting\\npath in seeds 1 and 3, at 5.43 and 5.56 ns. Seed 2 instead limits on\\nregister-file operand capture. The structural r6s1 forwarding retime,\\nr7s1 multiply bank, and r8s1 synchronous register file all regressed;\\nnone inserted a register between JALR target arithmetic and PC recovery.\\nThe r6s0 alignment precomputation also regressed, so this experiment\\nchanges execution latency rather than replicating alignment logic.\\nA dedicated target register could remove the complete live JALR operand\\ncone from redirect and squash control, at the cost of one extra execute\\ncycle for each JALR. Whether frequency gain exceeds that cost must be\\nmeasured; JALR frequency in the required timed workload is not assumed\\nto be zero.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The accepted r5s1 design reaches 409.80 fitness at 184.06 MHz. Its saved\\nrouted reports identify EX/MEM destination-tag comparison, operand\\nforwarding, and JALR target generation into the IF PC as the limiting\\npath in seeds 1 and 3, at 5.43 and 5.56 ns. Seed 2 instead limits on\\nregister-file operand capture. The structural r6s1 forwarding retime,\\nr7s1 multiply bank, and r8s1 synchronous register file all regressed;\\nnone inserted a register between JALR target arithmetic and PC recovery.\\nThe r6s0 alignment precomputation also regressed, so this experiment\\nchanges execution latency rather than replicating alignment logic.\\nA dedicated target register could remove the complete live JALR operand\\ncone from redirect and squash control, at the cost of one extra execute\\ncycle for each JALR. Whether frequency gain exceeds that cost must be\\nmeasured; JALR frequency in the required timed workload is not assumed\\nto be zero.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Give legal JALR a blocking, two-cycle EX path. Keep ordinary integer,\\nmultiply, load/store, conditional-branch, and direct-JAL execution at\\ntheir existing latency. Use the existing forwarding network and hold\\nthe JALR instruction in ID/EX until completion. This is one structural\\nexperiment in control-transfer execution, with no prediction state.\\n\\nOn the first unstalled EX edge, accept a valid, legal JALR exactly once.\\nCapture (forwarded_rs1 + immediate) modulo 2^32 with bit 0 cleared into\\na dedicated target register, capture the actual forwarded operands for\\nRVFI, and set a pending bit. Never capture a load address as its rs1\\noperand; respect the existing load-use interlock and unavailable-load\\nforwarding qualification. Launch requires the older EX/MEM owner to\\nbe able to advance. It must not depend on target alignment or a live\\ntarget-based redirect. Hold fetch and ID/EX on this launch cycle while\\nallowing older instructions to drain, emitting a control-zero EX/MEM\\nbubble when that register is available.\\n\\nDuring the following cycle, form JALR redirect_target and the alignment\\ndecision exclusively from the registered target. On the next available\\nEX/MEM edge, consume the pending operation once, emit its instruction\\nmetadata and PC+4 link, and redirect on that same edge if aligned. With\\nzero bus waits, completion is exactly one clock after launch, adding\\none cycle relative to the current JALR. Hold the target, saved operands,\\nand ID/EX owner if completion is blocked. Reset cancels pending work.\\nDo not allow live forwarding data or the current JALR adder output to\\nbypass the target register into PC, squash, trap, or link-write control.\\n\\nPreserve the current JALR semantics: bit 0 is cleared before alignment\\nchecking, target bit 1 causes the existing misalignment trap, a trapped\\nJALR suppresses its link and redirect and reports pc_next=PC+4, and an\\naligned JALR reports the registered target. A misaligned completion\\nreleases the held sequential fetch normally. Use saved launch operands\\nfor RVFI even after forwarding producers have drained; rd=rs1 and x0\\ncases must still use the pre-link source value. Illegal JALR encodings\\ncontinue through the existing illegal-instruction path without launch.\\n\\nAdd a separate JALR wait input to hazard control. It holds fetch and\\nID/EX without retiring or issuing the held instruction twice. Actual\\ndmem backpressure retains its current priority and preserves the older\\nrequest and WB forwarding payload. At aligned completion, clear the\\nJALR wait condition so redirect can flush the younger instruction and\\noverride an imem stall on the same edge. Restrict the existing live\\njump-resolution path to direct JAL; branch behavior is unchanged.\\nPreserve r5s1's separation between wide payload capture and bubble\\ncontrol, and retain control-zero invalid EX/MEM entries.\\n\\nCrucially, advance JALR into EX/MEM only when its registered redirect\\nis consumed. The r6s2 MEM-stage predictor experiment failed liveness;\\ndo not retire a jump first and redirect one stage later. The proposed\\nschedule delays JALR retirement together with its redirect, retaining\\nthe existing redirect-to-target-DIV/REM retirement spacing. Verify\\nthat bound with the unchanged formal gate and explicit JALR-to-DIV/REM\\nstreams; do not add divider cycles or relax the liveness window.\\n\\nForecast a low-confidence 3% fitness gain. For illustration, a 5% Fmax\\ngain with 2% more marker-window cycles yields approximately 2.94% more\\nfitness; these are targets, not measurements. Count timed JALRs and\\nmeasure actual extra cycles under identical stall seeds. Register-file,\\nALU-control, target-register input, or new hold-enable paths may become\\nlimiting, and added registers may worsen placement. Inspect all three\\nrouted seeds, including target-register input and output paths, without\\ntreating omitted timing arcs as zero delay or adding timing exceptions.\\n\\nPreserve nret=1, the external IO and RVFI contract, decoder defaults,\\narithmetic and ALTOPS formulas, divider schedule, direct normal-bank\\nmemory address, and every existing correctness gate. Run lint, unit\\ntests, unchanged formal, stalled ISS cosim, and three-seed FPGA fitness.\\nRequire the requested 6 KB CRCs and validation UART literal, bounded\\naccesses, and marker-only timing. Prior logs distinguish the evaluator's\\n2 KB fixture from supplemental 6 KB runs; keep those results distinct\\nand do not modify benchmark or evaluator files to reconcile them.\\nAccept only a measured increase in the unchanged fitness product.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the JALR target/operand capture registers and one pending owner\\nbit, with launch, wait, and completion control. Advance the held\\nJALR and redirect together using only the registered target; retain\\nsaved RVFI operands and precise misalignment/link suppression.\\nExclude JALR from live jump resolution. Preserve ordinary execution,\\ndivider ownership, direct memory addressing, payload capture policy,\\ndmem holds, and control-zero bubbles during the extra execute cycle.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Integrate JALR wait into fetch and ID/EX holding, while preserving\\nload-use, dmem, divider, and redirect priorities. Allow launch to\\ndrain the older EX/MEM owner once and completion to flush a younger\\ninstruction. Keep WB retention tied to actual memory backpressure.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect the new EX JALR-wait signal to hazard control. Preserve the\\nexisting redirect interface, pipeline retirement boundary, order\\ncounter, normal-bank memory address, and all nret=1 external ports.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_ex_result_banks.py\", \"description\": \"Add direct checks of JALR launch/completion ownership, registered\\ntarget isolation while live operands change, saved RVFI operands,\\nblocked completion, reset cancellation, aligned/misaligned targets,\\nand transitions among JALR, ordinary, divider, and bubble owners.\\nRetain all existing arithmetic, divider, and result-bank assertions.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add full ISS/RVFI comparisons for JALR with RF, EX/MEM, retained WB,\\nload, and divider producers; repeated destination writers; rd=rs1;\\nx0; negative immediates; aligned, bit-0-set, and bit-1-set targets;\\nconsecutive jumps; and JALR targets beginning with DIV/REM. Exercise\\nimem stalls at completion, long older-memory holds, reset while\\npending, and wrong-path loads/stores/divides. Require one ordered\\nretirement and no duplicate memory effects, exactly one added JALR\\nexecute cycle without stalls, unchanged ordinary/divider timing,\\nand the existing liveness bound. Update only internal timing and\\nownership expectations affected by the intentional JALR latency.\\n\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the JALR target/operand capture registers and one pending owner\\nbit, with launch, wait, and completion control. Advance the held\\nJALR and redirect together using only the registered target; retain\\nsaved RVFI operands and precise misalignment/link suppression.\\nExclude JALR from live jump resolution. Preserve ordinary execution,\\ndivider ownership, direct memory addressing, payload capture policy,\\ndmem holds, and control-zero bubbles during the extra execute cycle.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Integrate JALR wait into fetch and ID/EX holding, while preserving\\nload-use, dmem, divider, and redirect priorities. Allow launch to\\ndrain the older EX/MEM owner once and completion to flush a younger\\ninstruction. Keep WB retention tied to actual memory backpressure.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect the new EX JALR-wait signal to hazard control. Preserve the\\nexisting redirect interface, pipeline retirement boundary, order\\ncounter, normal-bank memory address, and all nret=1 external ports.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_ex_result_banks.py\", \"description\": \"Add direct checks of JALR launch/completion ownership, registered\\ntarget isolation while live operands change, saved RVFI operands,\\nblocked completion, reset cancellation, aligned/misaligned targets,\\nand transitions among JALR, ordinary, divider, and bubble owners.\\nRetain all existing arithmetic, divider, and result-bank assertions.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add full ISS/RVFI comparisons for JALR with RF, EX/MEM, retained WB,\\nload, and divider producers; repeated destination writers; rd=rs1;\\nx0; negative immediates; aligned, bit-0-set, and bit-1-set targets;\\nconsecutive jumps; and JALR targets beginning with DIV/REM. Exercise\\nimem stalls at completion, long older-memory holds, reset while\\npending, and wrong-path loads/stores/divides. Require one ordered\\nretirement and no duplicate memory effects, exactly one added JALR\\nexecute cycle without stalls, unchanged ordinary/divider timing,\\nand the existing liveness bound. Update only internal timing and\\nownership expectations affected by the intentional JALR latency.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 341.76, \"delta_pct\": -16.6, \"vs_baseline\": 20.84, \"fmax_mhz\": 153.99, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4505747, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5605, \"ff\": 2191, \"seeds\": [157.21, 153.99, 146.01], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-06T12:50:35.832285Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-06 hyp-20260906-002-r9s1 (regression, -16.60%): Inserting jalr_target_q after the full forwarding and addition cone shifted a critical path to its input while divider operand enables and EX result selection limited other seeds, reducing reported median Fmax 16.34% despite only 0.32% more 2 KB CoreMark cycles.\"}\n28:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260906-003-r9s2\", \"title\": \"Backward prediction with alignment-independent EX recovery control\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Earlier branch-only prediction reduced the evaluator's marker-window cycles\\nfrom 4,491,485 to 4,309,463, but r5s2 and r8s2 lost substantially more Fmax\\nthan they gained in throughput per clock. The r7s2 implementation notes\\nidentify forwarding/JALR alignment followed by repair/hold/squash to ID\\ncontrol RESET as the worst path in every seed. The r8s2 lesson also shows\\nthat reducing squash fanout to one valid bit did not shorten the upstream\\narithmetic cone. Target alignment still participates in the recovery\\ndecision through the shared misalign_fault signal. The full history also\\nrecords r6s2's MEM-stage validation failing liveness_ch0, so delaying all\\nrecovery is not an established solution under the unchanged checks.\\n\\nA misaligned control transfer can request an EX redirect to its existing\\narchitectural continuation, PC+4, while retaining the same trap and link\\nsuppression. This spends a conservative bubble on a trapping transfer\\nand allows recovery control to depend on decoded instruction class and\\nbranch outcome without waiting for target-alignment qualification.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Earlier branch-only prediction reduced the evaluator's marker-window cycles\\nfrom 4,491,485 to 4,309,463, but r5s2 and r8s2 lost substantially more Fmax\\nthan they gained in throughput per clock. The r7s2 implementation notes\\nidentify forwarding/JALR alignment followed by repair/hold/squash to ID\\ncontrol RESET as the worst path in every seed. The r8s2 lesson also shows\\nthat reducing squash fanout to one valid bit did not shorten the upstream\\narithmetic cone. Target alignment still participates in the recovery\\ndecision through the shared misalign_fault signal. The full history also\\nrecords r6s2's MEM-stage validation failing liveness_ch0, so delaying all\\nrecovery is not an established solution under the unchanged checks.\\n\\nA misaligned control transfer can request an EX redirect to its existing\\narchitectural continuation, PC+4, while retaining the same trap and link\\nsuppression. This spends a conservative bubble on a trapping transfer\\nand allows recovery control to depend on decoded instruction class and\\nbranch outcome without waiting for target-alignment qualification.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Implement one static backward-taken conditional-branch predictor with\\none-slot EX recovery whose squash strobe is independent of target\\nalignment. Keep ordinary execution and retirement boundaries unchanged.\\nThe new experiment is the separation of prediction-repair control from\\ntarget/trap data selection; the branch policy reuses the measured r5s2\\npolicy. JAL and JALR remain sequentially predicted. Do not add a BTB,\\nhistory table, return stack, delayed repair stage, or arithmetic shortcut.\\n\\nIn IF, predecode raw imem_data independently of flush, stall and redirect.\\nPredict taken only for opcode 0x63, funct3 0/1/4/5/6/7, a negative B\\ndisplacement, word-aligned fetch PC, and instruction bit 8 clear. These\\nconditions guarantee that a predicted branch target is aligned. Compute\\nits sign-extended B target with full 32-bit modulo arithmetic; compute\\nPC+4 independently. Select with raw prediction eligibility and apply the\\nselection only on the existing accepted fetch edge. Reset and EX repair\\nretain priority. Keep imem_addr directly driven by the PC register and\\npreserve the existing invalid/NOP behavior for discarded fetches.\\n\\nCarry predicted_taken with the accepted instruction into ID/EX. In ID,\\nadditionally register repair_invert = decoded branch_op[0] XOR\\npredicted_taken. Keep architectural branch_op unchanged. Treat these\\ntwo bits as ordinary payload: synchronous reset, normal capture enable,\\nand complete retention with a held owner. Their values are inert when\\nID/EX valid is zero. Retain the current control-zero invalid entries and\\nthe winner's separate control/payload capture domains; do not introduce\\nr8s2's raw-invalid-control representation or wide flush-dependent enables.\\n\\nEX shares equality, signed-less-than and unsigned-less-than predicates\\nfrom the existing forwarded operands. Select base_cond by architectural\\nbranch_op[2:1], using equality for BEQ/BNE and the respective less-than\\npredicate for the signed and unsigned pairs. Architectural branch\\ndirection uses original branch_op[0]. Direction mismatch uses the\\nregistered repair_invert, avoiding a serial extra XOR after direction\\nselection. Define the recovery request as:\\n\\n  branch_repair = in.ctrl.is_branch && (base_cond XOR in.repair_invert)\\n  redirect = in.valid && !reset && !in.ctrl.is_illegal\\n             && (in.ctrl.is_jump || branch_repair)\\n\\nHere is_illegal is the registered decoder result, never the dynamically\\naugmented ctrl_with_trap.is_illegal. Neither misalign_fault, target bits,\\ntarget adders, resolved pc_next, nor a full-next-PC equality check may\\nfeed the redirect strobe. No branch_repair_enable alignment qualifier\\nis needed: taken speculation was already restricted to aligned targets.\\nKeep recovery level-style through existing holds; do not insert a generic\\nEX-accept or div_wait qualifier into this strobe.\\n\\nPreserve existing branch/jump alignment detection, taken-only branch\\ntraps, JALR bit-zero clearing, and suppression of a trapped jump's link\\nwrite. These checks still govern architectural ctrl_with_trap and RVFI\\npc_next. Separately choose the recovery address. For a decoded jump,\\nselect jump_target when aligned and PC+4 when it traps. For a branch\\npredicted taken, the only repair is an exit, so select PC+4 directly\\nfrom the registered prediction bit. For a branch predicted not taken,\\nselect branch_target when aligned and PC+4 when the taken target traps.\\nThis branch target mux need not wait for the live branch comparison.\\nAll address bits and existing wraparound behavior remain architectural.\\n\\nIn particular, an unpredicted taken misaligned branch and a misaligned\\nlegal JAL/JALR now assert redirect to PC+4 and discard the younger slot.\\nThey retire exactly once with the same trap, suppressed link write and\\nresolved continuation as today. Never send the misaligned target to IF.\\nAn untaken misaligned branch still does not trap or repair. Reserved\\nbranches, illegal JALR encodings, and invalid entries cannot redirect.\\nCorrectly predicted legal branches have no bubble; an EX repair discards\\nexactly the one younger combinational fetch/decode slot without stalls.\\n\\nPreserve PC repair priority over imem unavailability and the existing\\ndmem/divider hold priority for the resolving owner. A held instruction\\nkeeps its operands and prediction until it advances. A repeated repair\\nduring that hold cannot duplicate retirement or a memory transaction.\\nYounger stores, loads and DIV/REM must be squashed before they acquire\\nan EX/MEM or divider owner. Retain existing EX/MEM control-zero bubbles,\\nheld MEM/WB forwarding data, divider completion-bank ownership and the\\ndirectly registered memory-address bank. No ALU/divider changes belong\\nto this predictor hypothesis.\\n\\nThe measurable timing claim is narrower than eliminating all carry\\npaths: target-alignment and JALR target arithmetic must cease to be\\ncombinational inputs of the squash strobe. Branch comparisons, the\\nrepair-address-to-PC path, ordinary load-use logic and placement remain\\npotential limits. Inspect mapped dependencies and all three routed\\nseeds, distinguishing repair control from repair target data; do not\\ninfer success merely from smaller fanout or source-level factoring.\\n\\nEstimate 3% greater fitness with low confidence. If the earlier 4.0526%\\ncycle saving survives and median Fmax loses 1%, the product improves\\nabout 3.18%. At 4,309,463 cycles, break-even is approximately 176.60 MHz\\nagainst the supplied 184.06 MHz, 409.80 iter/sec winner. These are\\nconditional forecasts, not measurements; target selection and other\\npaths may still outweigh the gain. Measure actual marker-window cycles,\\nmedian Fmax and resources with the unchanged evaluator. Preserve nret=1\\nand every hard invariant. Run unchanged lint, unit, formal including\\nliveness, ISS cosim, CRC/UART, OOB, marker and three-seed FPGA gates.\\nExplicitly test a misaligned transfer followed by DIV/REM against the\\nexisting progress bound; never change formal depths to accommodate it.\\nKeep the evaluator fixture authoritative and disclose any 2 KB/6 KB\\ndiscrepancy as prior notes do, without modifying the workload or gates.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted_taken to if_id_t and id_ex_t, and repair_invert to\\nid_ex_t. Document their instruction association and valid-qualified\\nuse. Preserve control-zero bubbles and the existing RVFI bundles.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the specified aligned backward-branch predecode, independent\\nfull-width target/PC+4 calculation and raw prediction mux. Export\\nprediction metadata with the fetched instruction; preserve current\\nPC enables, reset/repair priority and directly registered addressing.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture prediction and decode-folded repair polarity in the ordinary\\npayload domain, retaining both through holds. Keep original branch\\ncontrols, strict decoding and the winner's control-zero squash rules.\\nPrediction metadata must not introduce new dynamic payload resets.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement alignment-independent one-slot recovery using the shared\\nbranch predicates and registered repair polarity. All valid decoded\\njumps request recovery, including target traps; independently select\\nPC+4 for trap continuation. Preserve alignment faults, link-write\\nsuppression, actual RVFI pc_next, forwarding and divider ownership.\\nDo not compare resolved PCs or gate the strobe with augmented traps.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep the existing EX recovery wiring and top-level interface, updating\\ncomments to specify a repair request that also covers PC+4 trap\\ncontinuation. Preserve nret=1, memory-address and forwarding wiring.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Preserve existing one-slot EX squash and memory/divider hold priority.\\nDocument redirect as prediction repair or conservative trap recovery;\\ndo not requalify it with target alignment, resolved traps or a new\\nacceptance net. Verify unavailable imem cannot drop PC repair.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add fetch tests for branch funct3 validity, sign/alignment eligibility,\\nfull-width target carry/wrap, sequential prediction of all other\\nopcodes, changing stalled imem data and exact prediction acceptance.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_id_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Update bundle packing and check saved prediction/polarity, independent\\npayload capture, control-zero bubbles and complete held-owner\\nretention. Preserve existing decoding and operand assertions.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_ex_result_banks.py\", \"description\": \"Update ID/EX packing with sequential-prediction defaults. Preserve all\\narithmetic, result-bank, direct-address and forwarding checks; adapt\\njump-repair expectations only for the intentional PC+4 trap bubble,\\nretaining exact architectural trap/link/pc_next assertions.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check all branch conditions/outcomes, backward loops/exits, forwarded\\nand load-dependent comparisons, aligned and misaligned JAL/JALR,\\nillegal encodings, memory holds and imem stalls against the unchanged\\nISS. Distinguish zero-bubble correct prediction and one-slot repair.\\nFor misaligned taken transfers require a PC+4 recovery and unchanged\\ntrapping retirement/link suppression; untaken misaligned branches\\nremain sequential and nontrapping. Test consecutive trap repairs and\\na repaired successor that is DIV/REM, reset during holds, monotonic\\nRVFI order/PC continuity and no accepted wrong-path memory/divider\\naction. Preserve architectural assertions and existing formal bounds.\\n\"}]}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted_taken to if_id_t and id_ex_t, and repair_invert to\\nid_ex_t. Document their instruction association and valid-qualified\\nuse. Preserve control-zero bubbles and the existing RVFI bundles.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the specified aligned backward-branch predecode, independent\\nfull-width target/PC+4 calculation and raw prediction mux. Export\\nprediction metadata with the fetched instruction; preserve current\\nPC enables, reset/repair priority and directly registered addressing.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture prediction and decode-folded repair polarity in the ordinary\\npayload domain, retaining both through holds. Keep original branch\\ncontrols, strict decoding and the winner's control-zero squash rules.\\nPrediction metadata must not introduce new dynamic payload resets.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement alignment-independent one-slot recovery using the shared\\nbranch predicates and registered repair polarity. All valid decoded\\njumps request recovery, including target traps; independently select\\nPC+4 for trap continuation. Preserve alignment faults, link-write\\nsuppression, actual RVFI pc_next, forwarding and divider ownership.\\nDo not compare resolved PCs or gate the strobe with augmented traps.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep the existing EX recovery wiring and top-level interface, updating\\ncomments to specify a repair request that also covers PC+4 trap\\ncontinuation. Preserve nret=1, memory-address and forwarding wiring.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Preserve existing one-slot EX squash and memory/divider hold priority.\\nDocument redirect as prediction repair or conservative trap recovery;\\ndo not requalify it with target alignment, resolved traps or a new\\nacceptance net. Verify unavailable imem cannot drop PC repair.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add fetch tests for branch funct3 validity, sign/alignment eligibility,\\nfull-width target carry/wrap, sequential prediction of all other\\nopcodes, changing stalled imem data and exact prediction acceptance.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_id_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Update bundle packing and check saved prediction/polarity, independent\\npayload capture, control-zero bubbles and complete held-owner\\nretention. Preserve existing decoding and operand assertions.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_ex_result_banks.py\", \"description\": \"Update ID/EX packing with sequential-prediction defaults. Preserve all\\narithmetic, result-bank, direct-address and forwarding checks; adapt\\njump-repair expectations only for the intentional PC+4 trap bubble,\\nretaining exact architectural trap/link/pc_next assertions.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check all branch conditions/outcomes, backward loops/exits, forwarded\\nand load-dependent comparisons, aligned and misaligned JAL/JALR,\\nillegal encodings, memory holds and imem stalls against the unchanged\\nISS. Distinguish zero-bubble correct prediction and one-slot repair.\\nFor misaligned taken transfers require a PC+4 recovery and unchanged\\ntrapping retirement/link suppression; untaken misaligned branches\\nremain sequential and nontrapping. Test consecutive trap repairs and\\na repaired successor that is DIV/REM, reset during holds, monotonic\\nRVFI order/PC continuity and no accepted wrong-path memory/divider\\naction. Preserve architectural assertions and existing formal bounds.\\n\"}], \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 220.35, \"delta_pct\": -46.23, \"vs_baseline\": -22.09, \"fmax_mhz\": 94.96, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4309463, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5694, \"ff\": 2096, \"seeds\": [94.96, 97.51, 93.14], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"# Backward prediction with alignment-independent EX recovery control\\n\\nImplemented the proposed predictor and conservative PC+4 trap recovery in\\n`cores/bench`. Functional gates pass. The measured fitness regresses: **220.35\\niterations/second**, versus the supplied winner's 409.80. The predicted cycle\\nsaving survives, but the timing forecast does not.\\n\\n## Implementation\\n\\n- IF predecodes raw instruction data independently of stall, flush, and repair.\\n  Only legal conditional-branch funct3 values, negative B immediates, aligned\\n  fetch PCs, and instruction bit 8 clear predict taken. Separate full-width\\n  B-target and PC+4 additions feed the raw prediction mux. The existing PC\\n  register enable, reset/repair priority, directly registered imem address, and\\n  discarded-fetch invalid/NOP behavior remain intact. Prediction metadata is\\n  raw payload and is inert for an invalid fetch.\\n- IF/ID carries `predicted_taken`; ID/EX carries that bit and the decoded\\n  `branch_op[0] XOR predicted_taken` as `repair_invert`. Both use the existing\\n  synchronous-reset payload capture/hold domain. Architectural branch_op and\\n  the separate control-zero invalid/flush domain are unchanged.\\n- EX shares equality, signed-less-than, and unsigned-less-than predicates from\\n  the existing forwarded operands. Architectural direction uses branch_op[0];\\n  repair uses the registered repair_invert. The redirect equation is exactly\\n  valid AND NOT reset AND NOT registered decoder illegal AND (jump OR branch\\n  mismatch). It has no target-alignment, augmented-trap, resolved-PC,\\n  next-PC-equality, EX-accept, or divider-wait qualification.\\n- Recovery target selection is separate. Jumps use aligned jump_target or PC+4\\n  for a trap. Predicted-taken branch exits use PC+4 directly. Unpredicted\\n  branches select aligned branch_target or PC+4 without waiting for branch\\n  comparison. Taken-only branch traps, JALR bit-zero clearing, trapped-link\\n  suppression, and architectural RVFI pc_next remain unchanged.\\n- Existing hazard equations are unchanged. A repair discards the single\\n  younger combinational fetch/decode slot. Memory/divider holds retain the\\n  resolving owner; PC repair still overrides unavailable imem. No ALU/divider,\\n  result-bank, MEM/WB forwarding-data, direct memory-address, or retirement\\n  logic changed. `nret: 1` and all core ports remain unchanged.\\n\\nNo architectural deviations from the hypothesis. No BTB/history/return stack,\\ndelayed recovery, arithmetic shortcut, raw invalid controls, or new payload\\nflush/reset/enable domain was introduced.\\n\\n## Tests and unchanged gates\\n\\nValidation ran in an isolated copy under:\\n\\n`$TMPDIR/hyp-r9s2-validation`\\n\\nThe final RTL was byte-compared with this tested copy. Evaluator, formal\\nconfiguration/wrappers, FPGA scripts/wrapper, ISS/harness, Makefile, and\\ncore.yaml copies were also checked unchanged. No protected worktree source was\\nmodified. This root notes file is the explicitly requested implementation\\nwriteup and the path read by the orchestrator.\\n\\n- Required Verilator lint command: **PASS**, no warnings/errors.\\n- Local formal: **PASS on the first RTL attempt, 53 passed / 0 failed**.\\n  Executed unchanged `bash formal/run_all.sh` with `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl`,\\n  `CORE_NAME=bench`, `WRAPPER=formal/wrapper_si.sv`,\\n  `CHECKS_CFG=formal/checks_si.cfg`, and `JOBS=6` in the scratch copy. Includes\\n  liveness_ch0, PC continuity, unique order, illegal/trap, register, and all\\n  instruction checks. No formal fixes, retries, depth changes, or exclusions.\\n- Unit tests: all **10 pytest runners pass**. The full suite passed, followed\\n  by a passing rerun of the expanded pipeline suite. Final XMLs contain **153\\n  passing cocotb tests**, including **27 pipeline tests**. Real and ALTOPS ALU\\n  and EX-bank tests remain present.\\n- `python3 -m tools.eval.cosim . bench`: **PASS, 2 ELFs**. This includes the\\n  unchanged byte-exact selftest ISS comparison and stalled CoreMark CRC/UART\\n  validation. Pipeline protocol tests also compare against the unchanged ISS\\n  under directed holds and approximately 22% random stalls on both buses.\\n- `make fpga TARGET=bench`, with the existing single-retirement wrapper and\\n  harness selection: **all 3 routed seeds complete**, CoreMark completes, no\\n  OOB failure, CRC/UART and both timing markers accepted by the evaluator.\\n- Formal-deep was not run: multiplier/divider arithmetic was not modified;\\n  real arithmetic remains covered by the retained unit and ISS tests.\\n\\nAdded directed coverage checks all branch pairs/outcomes, backward loops and\\nexits, forwarded/load-dependent comparisons, branch funct3 reservations, every\\nother IF opcode, sign/alignment eligibility, full-width carry/wrap, changing\\nstalled fetch data, exact PC acceptance, complete prediction/polarity retention,\\nand separate control/payload capture. Tests distinguish zero-bubble correct\\npredictions from exactly one discarded repair slot. Legal misaligned JAL/JALR\\nand taken branches recover to PC+4 with the same trapping retirement and zero\\nlink write; untaken misaligned branches and reserved/illegal encodings do not\\nrepair. Consecutive traps, wrong-path loads/stores/DIV/REM, repeated repairs\\nduring older memory holds, unavailable imem, and reset during memory/divider\\nholds are covered. Accepted memory transactions and divider launches are\\nmatched to the retiring ISS stream, in addition to strict RVFI order/PC checks.\\n\\nIn particular, each of DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU immediately following a legal\\nmisaligned control transfer retires exactly **10 cycles** after the trap in the\\nzero-wait directed test. This meets the existing progress bound; no bound was\\nchanged. Consecutive trapping repairs followed by DIV/REM also pass.\\n\\nInitial test execution encountered a macOS embedded-Python dylib lookup issue;\\nit was resolved in the runner environment using the installed OSS CAD Python\\nand its library directory. Existing PyYAML/psutil packages were copied into\\nscratch dependencies for evaluator imports. No test or evaluator was weakened\\nto resolve these environment issues.\\n\\n## Measured result\\n\\nUnchanged evaluator workload: 10 iterations, -O3, --bench --istall --dstall.\\n\\n| Metric | Result |\\n| --- | ---: |\\n| Marker-window cycles | 4,309,463 |\\n| Cycle reduction from supplied 4,491,485 winner | 4.0526% |\\n| Seed 1 routed Fmax | 94.96 MHz |\\n| Seed 2 routed Fmax | 97.51 MHz |\\n| Seed 3 routed Fmax | 93.14 MHz |\\n| Median routed Fmax | 94.96 MHz |\\n| Median Fmax change from 184.06 MHz | -48.4081% |\\n| CoreMark fitness | 220.35 iter/sec |\\n| Fitness change from 409.80 iter/sec | -46.2293% |\\n| LUT4 | 5,694 (+204 versus supplied 5,490) |\\n| FF | 2,096 (-16 versus supplied 2,112) |\\n\\nThe evaluator's rounded `ipc_coremark` display is 0.000002; fitness uses the\\nunrounded ratio 10 / 4,309,463. The 3% gain estimate was a forecast, and is not\\nsupported by these measurements. The approximately 176.60 MHz break-even\\nfrequency is not reached.\\n\\n## Mapped dependencies and every routed seed\\n\\nInspected the actual evaluator-generated `synth.json` and all three final\\n`pnr_seed*/nextpnr.log` reports, cutting combinational fan-in at register and\\nsynchronous memory outputs. Synthesis absorbs the named redirect wire into\\nits consumers, so the mapped audit follows the actual ID control-reset,\\nID valid-data, ID control-data, and PC-enable endpoints. None contains an ALU\\ncell from the EX JALR target addition, branch/jump target addition, or EX PC+4\\naddition. The control-reset cone contains 396 combinational cells and 31 ALU\\ncells from the unsigned branch comparison (`rs1 < rs2`), with zero target-adder\\ncells. The ID valid-data and PC-enable cones also contain the comparison carry\\nchain and zero target-adder cells. The full ID control-data cone likewise has\\nno target-adder dependency.\\n\\nRepair address data remains arithmetic: the PC data cone includes 32 JALR\\nadder cells, 32 branch/jump target adder cells, and 30 EX PC+4 cells, in addition\\nto IF prediction/PC+4 arithmetic and branch comparison. This confirms the\\nrequested separation of target/alignment from squash control, not elimination\\nof arithmetic from the PC path.\\n\\n- Seed 1: EX/MEM register -> forwarding selection -> unsigned branch\\n  comparison carry chain -> recovery/hold/squash ->\\n  `cpu.u_id.reg_q_DFFRE_Q_177.RESET`. The reported path traverses 26 comparator\\n  ALU cells. Delay: 4.89 ns logic + 5.64 ns routing = 10.53 ns.\\n- Seed 2: the corresponding forwarding/comparison/recovery path ends at\\n  `cpu.u_id.reg_q_DFFRE_Q_178.RESET`, traversing 25 comparator ALU cells.\\n  Delay: 4.84 ns logic + 5.42 ns routing = 10.26 ns.\\n- Seed 3: EX/MEM register -> forwarding and LUT comparison/recovery/decode\\n  logic -> `cpu.u_id.reg_q_DFFRE_Q_165.D`. The reported path contains 8 LUT4s\\n  and 4 MUX2_LUT5s, with no ALU carry cell on that particular path. Delay:\\n  4.73 ns logic + 6.01 ns routing = 10.74 ns.\\n\\nAll three start at `cpu.u_ex.reg_q_DFFR_Q_24.Q`, the EX/MEM destination-register\\nbit used in forwarding selection. Target alignment/JALR target arithmetic has\\nleft the mapped squash cone, but comparison, forwarding, recovery/decode\\nlogic, and routing still dominate. Reduced alignment dependence is therefore\\na verified structural result, not a fitness improvement.\\n\\n## Authoritative fixture discrepancy and evidence\\n\\nThe prompt/CLAUDE description says 6 KB and CRCs d4b0/be52/5e47. The unchanged\\nevaluator and default bench Makefile actually use **2 KB**, with expected\\nseedcrc=e9f5, crclist=e714, crcmatrix=1fd7, crcstate=8e3a, crcfinal=fcaf. The\\ncore_portme.h fallback is 6000, but the Makefile's `COREMARK_SIZE ?= 2000`\\noverrides it. The supplied benchmark-run ELF was used as the authoritative\\nfixture; neither workload nor gates were changed. These results are 2 KB\\nmeasurements, not a claim that the stated 6 KB workload was measured.\\n\\nAuthoritative coremark.elf SHA-256:\\n`4c2544002169271a2349ebfb6bf4fcaf1201a26580b51fdb0d4eb48e877f1383`.\\n\\nScratch evidence: `formal-check.log`, `unit-check.log`, `pipeline-check.log`,\\n`cosim-check.log`, `fpga-check.log`, and `mapped-routed-dependencies.json`\\n(mapped endpoint audit, all routed critical paths, test counts, and final RTL\\nhashes), plus the three routed JSON/netlist/log directories under\\n`cores/bench/generated/`. Passing local gates does not mark this hypothesis\\naccepted; the unchanged orchestrator still makes that decision.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-06T12:46:52.630563Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-06 hyp-20260906-003-r9s2 (regression, -46.23%): Removing target-alignment/JALR adders from EX squash control still left EX/MEM rd-driven forwarding through branch-comparison carry chains (two seeds) and recovery/decode LUTs (third seed) dominating routed timing, cutting median Fmax 48.41% despite backward prediction's 4.05% reduction in 2 KB CoreMark cycles.\"}\n31:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260906-003-r10s2\", \"title\": \"Backward prediction with balanced EX comparison\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The predictor experiments repeatedly save instructions' fetch slots but\\nlose more Fmax than they gain in cycles. The branch-only policy in r5s2,\\nr8s2 and r9s2 reduced the recorded marker window from 4,491,485 to\\n4,309,463 cycles, a 4.0526% reduction. In r9s2, removing target-alignment\\narithmetic from recovery still produced only 94.96 MHz: two routed\\ncritical paths started at EX/MEM destination bits, passed through\\nforwarding and 25-26 branch-comparison carry cells, and reached ID\\ncontrol reset. The third was limited by comparison/recovery/decode LUTs.\\nR8s2 shows that reducing squash fanout alone does not fix this path.\\n\\nThe next predictor should directly shorten the branch predicate feeding\\nEX repair. A balanced Boolean comparison tree is an untested way to\\nremove the serial magnitude-comparison carry chain while retaining the\\nmeasured prediction policy and its one-slot recovery. Moving recovery\\nto MEM is unattractive here because r6s2 failed the unchanged liveness\\ncheck. These cycle figures are historical evaluator results, identified\\nin the implementation logs as the 2 KB fixture, not new 6 KB measurements.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The predictor experiments repeatedly save instructions' fetch slots but\\nlose more Fmax than they gain in cycles. The branch-only policy in r5s2,\\nr8s2 and r9s2 reduced the recorded marker window from 4,491,485 to\\n4,309,463 cycles, a 4.0526% reduction. In r9s2, removing target-alignment\\narithmetic from recovery still produced only 94.96 MHz: two routed\\ncritical paths started at EX/MEM destination bits, passed through\\nforwarding and 25-26 branch-comparison carry cells, and reached ID\\ncontrol reset. The third was limited by comparison/recovery/decode LUTs.\\nR8s2 shows that reducing squash fanout alone does not fix this path.\\n\\nThe next predictor should directly shorten the branch predicate feeding\\nEX repair. A balanced Boolean comparison tree is an untested way to\\nremove the serial magnitude-comparison carry chain while retaining the\\nmeasured prediction policy and its one-slot recovery. Moving recovery\\nto MEM is unattractive here because r6s2 failed the unchanged liveness\\ncheck. These cycle figures are historical evaluator results, identified\\nin the implementation logs as the 2 KB fixture, not new 6 KB measurements.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Implement one static backward-taken conditional-branch predictor with\\na balanced Boolean EX predicate network. The experimental distinction\\nfrom r9s2 is the implementation of branch comparison: replace its native\\nfull-width relational operators with explicit parallel small comparisons\\nand a balanced significance tree. Keep recovery in EX with the existing\\npipeline depth and one discarded younger fetch/decode slot per repair.\\nThis is one predictor experiment; its comparator is shared by prediction\\nvalidation and architectural branch resolution.\\n\\nAdd a combinational branch_compare module taking the existing forwarded\\n32-bit rs1 and rs2 and producing equal, less_unsigned and less_signed.\\nForm sixteen independent two-bit summaries using Boolean expressions.\\nFor each two-bit slice, with h the more significant bit and l the lower:\\n\\n  E = XNOR(a[h], b[h]) AND XNOR(a[l], b[l])\\n  L = (NOT a[h] AND b[h]) OR\\n      (XNOR(a[h], b[h]) AND NOT a[l] AND b[l])\\n\\nMerge adjacent high/low summaries with E = E_high AND E_low and\\nL = L_high OR (E_high AND L_low). Explicitly construct balanced levels\\nof 16, 8, 4, 2 and 1 summaries; never accumulate serially across slices.\\nThe root supplies equal and less_unsigned. Obtain less_signed as\\n(a[31] XOR b[31]) ? a[31] : less_unsigned. This preserves all RV32\\nsigned/unsigned cases, including equality and opposite-sign operands.\\nUse no full-width subtract, relational operator, or inferred ripple\\nrecurrence in this branch module. Do not change ALU SLT/SLTU, arithmetic,\\noperand forwarding selection, or the divider. Let normal synthesis map\\nthe Boolean tree to LUTs; do not rely on false-path or timing exceptions.\\n\\nIn IF, independently predecode raw imem_data for opcode 0x63 and legal\\nfunct3 values 0, 1, 4, 5, 6 and 7. Predict taken only for a negative\\nB-immediate, word-aligned fetch PC, and instruction bit 8 clear. Compute\\nthe full 32-bit sign-extended B target and PC+4 independently, preserving\\nmodulo-2^32 arithmetic. Raw eligibility selects their data mux; stalls,\\nflushes and acceptance must not feed that select. Apply this next PC\\nonly on the ordinary accepted fetch edge. Reset and EX repair retain\\npriority, and imem_addr remains directly driven by the PC register.\\nJAL, JALR and all other instructions predict sequentially. No target\\ntable, training state or return stack is needed.\\n\\nCarry predicted_taken with the exact accepted instruction into ID/EX.\\nAlso register repair_invert = decoded branch_op[0] XOR predicted_taken.\\nThese metadata bits use the winner's ordinary payload capture/hold\\ndomain, with synchronous reset and no dynamic payload squash. Preserve\\ncontrol-zero invalid entries and the separate control/payload domains.\\nHeld instructions retain their complete prediction and operand metadata.\\n\\nSelect base_cond from the shared comparison outputs: equal for BEQ/BNE,\\nless_signed for BLT/BGE, and less_unsigned for BLTU/BGEU. Architectural\\nbranch_cond is base_cond XOR the original branch_op[0]. Use the decoded\\nrepair polarity for the misprediction term, without another comparison:\\n\\n  branch_repair = in.ctrl.is_branch AND\\n                  (base_cond XOR in.repair_invert)\\n  redirect = in.valid AND NOT reset AND NOT in.ctrl.is_illegal AND\\n             (in.ctrl.is_jump OR branch_repair)\\n\\nHere is_illegal is the registered decoder result. Keep target alignment,\\ntarget addition, augmented trap control, full-next-PC equality, div_wait\\nand generic EX-accept qualification outside this repair strobe. Preserve\\nthe existing authoritative decoder and all misalignment detection.\\nBranch/jump target computation, JALR bit-zero clearing, trap propagation,\\ntrapped-link suppression and actual RVFI pc_next remain architectural.\\nFor a predicted-taken branch's repair select PC+4; for an unpredicted\\nbranch's repair select its aligned target or PC+4 on a target trap.\\nFor a jump select its aligned target or PC+4 on a target trap. Select\\nthis repair address independently of the live branch comparison.\\n\\nAs in the validated r9s2 protocol, a legal misaligned taken transfer\\nconservatively repairs to PC+4 and discards one younger slot, while\\nretiring once with the existing trap and suppressed link write. An\\nuntaken misaligned branch neither traps nor repairs. Reserved branch\\nencodings and illegal JALR instructions never redirect. Correctly\\npredicted branches introduce no bubble. Retain repair priority over\\nunavailable imem and the existing dmem/divider hold priority. Repeated\\nrepair while an owner is held must not duplicate execution or retirement.\\nSquash younger memory operations and DIV/REM before they acquire an\\nowner. Preserve held MEM/WB forwarding data, control-zero EX/MEM bubbles,\\ndivider result-bank ownership and the direct registered memory address.\\n\\nEstimate 3% greater fitness with low confidence. If the historical 4.0526%\\ncycle reduction repeats and median Fmax loses 1%, fitness improves about\\n3.18%. At 4,309,463 cycles, approximately 176.61 MHz is needed to beat\\nthe supplied 409.80 iter/sec winner. This is a forecast: LUT depth,\\nrouting, forwarding, JALR repair-address data or IF target selection\\ncould still prevent that frequency. Inspect the mapped branch network\\nto establish that its magnitude comparisons contain no ALU carry chain,\\nthen inspect every routed seed for the resulting predicate-to-recovery\\ndepth and any displaced critical paths. Source-level balance alone\\nis not evidence of faster hardware.\\n\\nRun unchanged lint, unit, formal including liveness, ISS cosim, CRC/UART,\\nOOB, marker-window, resource and three-seed FPGA checks. Explicitly check\\na repaired transfer followed by DIV/REM against the existing liveness\\nbound; never change formal depths. Report actual cycles, median Fmax,\\nLUT4/FF use and their resulting fitness against the same workload build.\\nPreserve nret=1 and every evaluation invariant. Disclose any fixture\\nsize discrepancy without modifying the evaluator or benchmark sources.\\nAll proposed edits are confined to cores/bench RTL and its unit tests.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_compare.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the Boolean two-bit comparison leaves and explicit balanced\\nsignificance tree. Export full-width equality, unsigned less-than\\nand signed less-than with no full-width arithmetic comparison.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted_taken to if_id_t and id_ex_t and repair_invert to\\nid_ex_t. Keep architectural controls, retirement width and resolved\\nRVFI bundles unchanged; document metadata ownership through holds.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add aligned backward-branch predecode, full-width independent target\\nand PC+4 calculation, and raw prediction selection. Export prediction\\nmetadata while preserving PC enables, repair priority, direct imem\\naddressing and discarded-fetch NOP/valid behavior.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture prediction and decode-folded repair polarity in the existing\\npayload domain. Preserve strict decode, control-zero bubbles and\\ncomplete owner retention during memory and divider holds.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use branch_compare for every branch predicate and share its outputs\\nbetween architectural direction and prediction repair. Implement\\nthe specified one-slot, alignment-independent repair strobe with\\nseparate architectural target/trap selection. Preserve all existing\\nforwarding, ALU/divider, link, result-bank and memory-address logic.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_branch_compare.py\", \"description\": \"Exhaust all two-bit input pairs and check full-width comparisons\\nagainst Python signed/unsigned references. Exercise equal operands,\\nevery most-significant-differing-bit position with adversarial lower\\nbits, each tree boundary, opposite signs, extrema and random pairs.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Test legal and reserved branch encodings, sign/alignment eligibility,\\nfull-address carry/wrap, sequential prediction of other opcodes,\\nstalled instruction-data changes and exact accepted prediction.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_id_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Update bundle packing and check prediction/polarity association,\\ncontrol-zero squashes, independent payload capture and held-owner\\nretention without weakening existing decode or operand assertions.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_ex_result_banks.py\", \"description\": \"Update ID/EX packing with sequential-prediction defaults. Preserve\\nall real/ALTOPS arithmetic, forwarding, direct-address and ownership\\nassertions; check exact branch predicates across forwarding sources\\nand the specified PC+4 repair on a trapping control transfer.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Validate all six branch conditions, backward loops/exits, forward\\ntaken branches, ALU/load-forwarded operands, JAL/JALR and misaligned\\ntransfers against the unchanged ISS under zero-wait and random bus\\nstalls. Check one-slot repair versus bubble-free correct prediction,\\nreset and long holds, repaired-transfer-to-DIV/REM progress, exact\\nRVFI PC/order/trap/link behavior, and absence of accepted wrong-path\\nmemory or divider operations. Retain every existing assertion.\\n\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_compare.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the Boolean two-bit comparison leaves and explicit balanced\\nsignificance tree. Export full-width equality, unsigned less-than\\nand signed less-than with no full-width arithmetic comparison.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted_taken to if_id_t and id_ex_t and repair_invert to\\nid_ex_t. Keep architectural controls, retirement width and resolved\\nRVFI bundles unchanged; document metadata ownership through holds.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add aligned backward-branch predecode, full-width independent target\\nand PC+4 calculation, and raw prediction selection. Export prediction\\nmetadata while preserving PC enables, repair priority, direct imem\\naddressing and discarded-fetch NOP/valid behavior.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture prediction and decode-folded repair polarity in the existing\\npayload domain. Preserve strict decode, control-zero bubbles and\\ncomplete owner retention during memory and divider holds.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use branch_compare for every branch predicate and share its outputs\\nbetween architectural direction and prediction repair. Implement\\nthe specified one-slot, alignment-independent repair strobe with\\nseparate architectural target/trap selection. Preserve all existing\\nforwarding, ALU/divider, link, result-bank and memory-address logic.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_branch_compare.py\", \"description\": \"Exhaust all two-bit input pairs and check full-width comparisons\\nagainst Python signed/unsigned references. Exercise equal operands,\\nevery most-significant-differing-bit position with adversarial lower\\nbits, each tree boundary, opposite signs, extrema and random pairs.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Test legal and reserved branch encodings, sign/alignment eligibility,\\nfull-address carry/wrap, sequential prediction of other opcodes,\\nstalled instruction-data changes and exact accepted prediction.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_id_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Update bundle packing and check prediction/polarity association,\\ncontrol-zero squashes, independent payload capture and held-owner\\nretention without weakening existing decode or operand assertions.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_ex_result_banks.py\", \"description\": \"Update ID/EX packing with sequential-prediction defaults. Preserve\\nall real/ALTOPS arithmetic, forwarding, direct-address and ownership\\nassertions; check exact branch predicates across forwarding sources\\nand the specified PC+4 repair on a trapping control transfer.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Validate all six branch conditions, backward loops/exits, forward\\ntaken branches, ALU/load-forwarded operands, JAL/JALR and misaligned\\ntransfers against the unchanged ISS under zero-wait and random bus\\nstalls. Check one-slot repair versus bubble-free correct prediction,\\nreset and long holds, repaired-transfer-to-DIV/REM progress, exact\\nRVFI PC/order/trap/link behavior, and absence of accepted wrong-path\\nmemory or divider operations. Retain every existing assertion.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 181.44, \"delta_pct\": -55.72, \"vs_baseline\": -35.85, \"fmax_mhz\": 78.19, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4309463, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5642, \"ff\": 2118, \"seeds\": [83.98, 78.19, 76.68], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"# Backward prediction with balanced EX comparison\\n\\nImplemented the requested predictor and Boolean comparator. Local correctness checks pass, but the measured FPGA fitness regresses: **181.44 iter/sec**, versus the supplied **409.80 iter/sec** winner. The cycle saving repeats; the frequency forecast does not.\\n\\n## Implementation\\n\\n- Added `cores/bench/rtl/branch_compare.sv`: sixteen independent two-bit Boolean E/L leaves and explicit 16 -> 8 -> 4 -> 2 -> 1 significance levels. Equality and unsigned less-than come from the root; signed less-than uses the operand sign difference. There is no data subtraction, full-width relational operator, or serial slice recurrence in this module.\\n- IF predecodes raw `imem_data` for opcode `0x63`, funct3 0/1/4/5/6/7, negative B-immediate, word-aligned PC and instruction bit 8 clear. Independent 32-bit target and PC+4 additions feed a mux selected only by raw eligibility. The existing PC register enable, synchronous reset, repair priority, direct imem address and discarded-fetch NOP/valid behavior remain.\\n- Added `predicted_taken` to IF/ID and ID/EX, and `repair_invert = decoded branch_op[0] XOR predicted_taken` to ID/EX. Both registered metadata bits use the existing payload capture/hold domain with synchronous reset and no flush reset. Invalid entries still have zero controls. Raw prediction metadata on discarded IF bundles is inactive because their validity/control is zero.\\n- EX shares the comparison outputs between architectural branch resolution and repair. The repair strobe uses valid, reset, registered decoder legality, jump control and the specified decoded polarity. Target arithmetic/alignment, augmented trap control, div_wait and EX acceptance do not qualify this strobe.\\n- Repair address selection is independent of the live comparison: a predicted branch repairs to PC+4; an unpredicted branch or jump repairs to its target, or PC+4 when the target is misaligned. Architectural target alignment, JALR bit-zero clearing, traps, suppressed trapped links and resolved RVFI PC remain intact. A legal misaligned taken transfer repairs once on advancement, discards one younger slot and retires with a trap; an untaken misaligned branch neither repairs nor traps.\\n- Added comparator and IF unit suites; extended ID, EX and pipeline suites. Updated packed bundle layouts and explicit simulator source lists. Divider launch checking now uses its actual ID/EX owner's PC instead of reconstructing ownership from speculative fetch PC minus four. Existing assertions were retained.\\n\\nNo architectural deviation from the hypothesis. ALU SLT/SLTU, arithmetic, forwarding selection, divider, memory/writeback ownership, direct registered dmem address, pipeline depth, top-level ports and `nret: 1` are unchanged. No timing exceptions, mapping attributes, evaluator changes or benchmark source changes were introduced. This root notes file is the explicit instruction-5 output and the location consumed by the orchestrator.\\n\\n## Local correctness results\\n\\n- Requested exact lint command passed without warnings:\\n  `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`.\\n- All **11 pytest runners / 153 cocotb test cases** passed, including real and ALTOPS ALU/EX suites. Tests were run in two batches: all non-pipeline runners, then the pipeline runner after its additions. Pipeline has 27 passing cases. XML reports are under `cores/bench/test/`.\\n- **Local formal status: PASS, first invocation, 53 passed / 0 failed, zero RTL fix attempts.** Ran the unchanged `bash formal/run_all.sh` with `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=6`; its ordinary nret autodetection selected `wrapper_si.sv` and `checks_si.cfg`. Liveness, unique, PC, register, instruction and illegal checks passed. No counterexample and no channel-zero PREUNSAT occurred. The liveness configuration remains `1 10 20`; no formal depths were changed.\\n- Directed tests cover repaired BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU/JAL/JALR immediately followed by each DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU. Under zero wait, the retirement gap is **exactly 10 cycles**, within the unchanged liveness interval. Correctly predicted backward branches have a one-cycle retirement spacing to the loop body; loop exits discard exactly one slot and have two-cycle spacing to an ordinary successor.\\n- Comparator coverage includes all 16 two-bit input pairs at every slice with three equal surrounding patterns; every most-significant differing bit with adversarial lower bits; tree boundaries, equal operands, signed extrema, opposite signs and 4,096 deterministic random pairs. EX tests exercise all six branch conditions and both prediction polarities through all combinations of the three forwarding sources.\\n- Pipeline tests compare with the **unchanged ISS and RVFI comparison function** under zero-wait and random approximately 22% bus stalls. They cover all branch directions, backward loops/exits, forward transfers, ALU/load forwarding, reserved branch encodings, illegal JALR, misaligned transfers and link suppression. Separate accepted-memory and divider-launch accounting detects wrong-path effects and duplicated ownership. Directed 11-15 cycle memory holds exercise held MEM/WB operands, repeated repair, prediction retention, unavailable imem priority and reset of a held repair.\\n- Unchanged `tools.eval.cosim` passed both fixture ELFs: selftest full RVFI comparison and CoreMark CRC validation. Additional native-harness selftest comparison passed **115 retirements** with zero wait and with `--istall --dstall`.\\n- The unchanged channel-zero RVFI guard passed. CoreMark reached EBREAK with `maxcycles_hit=false`, `oob=false`, valid start/stop markers and the literal `Correct operation validated.`.\\n- Fast formal uses the existing ALTOPS setting. Real arithmetic passed its existing unit suites and ISS cases; `formal-deep` was not run because no arithmetic implementation changed.\\n\\nThe formal runner normally writes through the worktree's shared `formal/riscv-formal` symlink. To keep its scratch writes isolated, the runner, wrappers, configs, framework checks and RTL were copied unchanged under the supplied TMPDIR before execution. Final RTL and every copied formal/config file were byte-compared with the validated inputs. No protected worktree file was edited. The installed Conda Python supplied pytest/cocotb/YAML/click dependencies.\\n\\n## Workload and fitness\\n\\n**Fixture discrepancy:** the prompt describes 6 KB, but the unchanged Makefile defaults to `TOTAL_DATA_SIZE=2000` and the unchanged evaluator checks 2 KB CRCs. The actual fixture prints `2K performance run parameters` and size 666 per algorithm. These are **2 KB measurements**, not 6 KB measurements; the prompt's 6 KB CRC set was not validated or substituted into the evaluator.\\n\\nCandidate and original winner RTL from worktree HEAD `2744aebfff761738b0795b7f7c2c11648dd4cc80` were simulated against the exact same supplied fixture ELF, SHA-256:\\n\\n`2646a2933b6a9142988d36cf1ef08e7ffd3c731d504a7206cd953dd9c42fe0f9`\\n\\nAn independent scratch rebuild with the unchanged benchmark Makefile used `-O3`, `-march=rv32im`, `-mabi=ilp32`, `TOTAL_DATA_SIZE=2000`, and the unchanged `ITERATIONS=10`. Both PT_LOAD segments, their addresses, sizes and ELF entry matched the supplied fixture exactly. The full ELF hash differs due to non-loaded metadata. The UART's `Compiler flags: -O2 -march=rv32im` is a hardcoded string in `core_portme.h`, not the actual rebuild command. Neither the scored ELF nor benchmark sources were replaced by this verification rebuild.\\n\\nBoth measured runs used `--bench --istall --dstall` and passed the unchanged UART validator: seedcrc `e9f5`, crclist `e714`, crcmatrix `1fd7`, crcstate `8e3a`, crcfinal `fcaf`, iterations 10.\\n\\n| Measurement | Original winner RTL | Candidate |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| Start marker cycle | 15,801 | 15,406 |\\n| Stop marker cycle | 4,507,286 | 4,324,869 |\\n| Marker-window cycles | 4,491,485 | 4,309,463 |\\n| Median Fmax, MHz | 184.06 supplied | 78.19 measured |\\n| LUT4 | 5,490 supplied | 5,642 measured |\\n| FF | 2,112 supplied | 2,118 measured |\\n| Fitness, iter/sec | 409.80 supplied | 181.44 measured |\\n\\nThe winner's cycles were remeasured locally; its FPGA frequency/resource values are the supplied winner values and were not rerouted. Candidate cycles decrease by **182,022 / 4.0526018%**. Fitness uses the unrounded ratio: `78.19e6 * 10 / 4309463 = 181.4379193 iter/sec`, a **55.7253% regression** versus 409.80. Approximately **176.6018 MHz** would be needed to tie 409.80 at this cycle count. The evaluator's rounded `ipc_coremark: 2e-06` was not used to recompute fitness.\\n\\n## Mapped and routed evidence\\n\\nRan the unchanged `fpga/scripts/synth.tcl` with the nret=1 FPGA wrapper and unchanged `tools.eval.fpga`, which runs `nextpnr_run.sh` for seeds 1/2/3. All three routed successfully. Each reports 5,642 LUT4 (27% of device capacity, below the 10,000 target) and 2,118 FF (13%). Synthesis's eight warnings are existing divider array-to-register lowering notices; strict Verilator lint has none.\\n\\n| Seed | Final routed MHz | Critical delay, ns | Logic, ns | Routing, ns | Source -> sink |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\\n| 1 | 83.98 | 11.91 | 5.51 | 6.40 | ID/EX source-address alias `id_ex_w[20]` -> ID control RESET |\\n| 2 | 78.19 | 12.79 | 5.11 | 7.68 | MEM/WB destination alias `rvfi_insn_0[7]` -> ID control RESET |\\n| 3 | 76.68 | 13.04 | 5.51 | 7.53 | ID/EX source-address alias `id_ex_w[20]` -> ID control RESET |\\n\\nInspected every reported routed critical path and joined its cells to the authoritative mapped `synth.json`. Every path contains **16 combinational mapped cells: 11 LUT4 and 5 MUX2_LUT5, zero Gowin ALU carry cells**. All three pass through forwarding and the comparison/recovery/decode cone to ID reset. None displaced the reported worst path to IF target selection, JALR target addition or the divider recurrence. The endpoints are `cpu.u_id.reg_q_DFFRE_Q_180.RESET`, `_176.RESET`, and `_177.RESET`, respectively.\\n\\nTraversed the complete integrated ID-control-reset input cone back to registered/primary-input boundaries: 397 mapped cells, comprising 75 LUT4, 209 LUT3, 28 LUT2, 8 LUT1, 76 MUX2_LUT5 and one GND; **no ALU carry primitive anywhere in that cone**. Thus removal of the branch magnitude carry path is established in the integrated mapping, not inferred solely from source syntax. Some autogenerated net names contain `ALU` or `div` because of mapping/renaming; their actual cell types on the critical path are LUT/mux primitives.\\n\\nSupplementary standalone mapping of the unchanged `branch_compare` also contains no ALU cells: 45 LUT4, 3 LUT3, 5 LUT1, 8 MUX2_LUT5, one GND, plus I/O buffers. Maximum mapped LUT/mux depths from input buffers are equality 5, unsigned less-than 6 and signed less-than 7. These isolated depths are not a frequency claim: synthesis merges/renames logic in the full core, and the routed 16-cell path includes forwarding, predicate, repair and decode logic.\\n\\nThe experiment therefore removed the carry comparison without improving hardware speed. The remaining LUT depth and routing cost dominate and more than cancel the measured prediction benefit. Keep this as a functionally passing but fitness-regressing experiment; do not describe the estimated 3% gain as achieved.\\n\\n## Evidence locations\\n\\nValidation scratch root:\\n\\n`$TMPDIR/r10s2-validation-entdg92w`\\n\\n- `formal-check.log`: 53/0 summary; `formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-87898/checks/` contains all individual logs and unchanged generated checks.\\n- `cosim-eval.json`, `fpga-eval.json`, `synthesis.log`, `cosim-build.log`.\\n- `candidate-coremark.jsonl`, `winner-coremark.jsonl`: raw final UART/OOB/marker records.\\n- `cores/bench/generated/synth.json`, `pnr_seed{1,2,3}/nextpnr.log`, and each routed `pnr.json`.\\n- `comparator-map.log`, `cores/bench/generated/branch-compare-only.json`.\\n- `fixture-rebuild.log` and `fixture-rebuild/bench/programs/coremark.elf` document the independent O3/2 KB executable-content verification.\\n- Unit batch stdout: `$TMPDIR/r10s2-unit.log` and `$TMPDIR/r10s2-pipeline.log`; per-runner XML is in the allowed core test directory.\\n\\nAll spawned validation processes completed successfully. Protected sources, evaluation invariants and formal depths remain unchanged. Acceptance remains the orchestrator's decision.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-06T13:43:44.206212Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-06 hyp-20260906-003-r10s2 (regression, -55.72%): A balanced Boolean tree in branch_compare.sv eliminated branch-comparison carry cells but left a 16-cell LUT/mux path through forwarding and EX repair to ID control RESET in all three routed seeds, showing that carry removal alone cannot ensure faster recovery: median Fmax fell to 78.19 MHz despite 4.05% fewer 2 KB CoreMark cycles.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
