{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n    r=json.loads(line)\n    if r.get('id') == 'hyp-20260906-002-r5s1':\n        print(r['id'],r['title'],r['delta_pct'])\n        h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n        print(h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nprint('HYPOTHESIS_DIR',Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses').exists())\nprint('EXISTING_TARGET',Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260906-001-r13s0.yaml').exists())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260906-002-r5s1 Separate pipeline payload storage from bubble and divide control 7.14\nRestructure the existing ID/EX and EX/MEM boundaries into independently\nupdated payload and control banks. Bubble insertion should clear valid\nand the complete control word, while wide payload registers retain\ntheir normal capture/hold behavior. This is one pipeline-storage change:\npreserve the pipeline depth, instruction dispatch schedule, arithmetic,\nforwarding priority, and existing eight-clock divider protocol.\n\nIn ID, retain the exact reset/flush/stall precedence for valid and ctrl.\nCapture a decoded control word only with a valid incoming instruction;\nan accepted invalid input installs zero control and valid=0. Separate\npc, instr, immediates, source values and register addresses from that\nbubble-clearing bank. Give the payload its existing synchronous reset\nto zero, followed by capture when !stall and retention when stalled.\nFlush must not appear in the payload reset, data mux, or write enable.\nIn particular, a simultaneous load-use stall and flush clears control\nwhile retaining inactive payload; a dmem or division hold preserves\nthe complete active instruction. A redirect may capture discarded\npayload, but it must install an invalid, control-zero entry.\n\nIn EX, preserve the current control-bank transitions: reset clears it;\ndmem stall holds it; otherwise div_wait or !in.valid installs a bubble;\notherwise capture ctrl_with_trap and valid. Preserve the registered\ndivider-bank selector and its ownership rules. Independently capture\nthe normal ALU-or-PC+4 result and instruction payload on every !stall\nedge, with synchronous reset to zero. Allow this normal result bank to\nupdate during invalid cycles, divide computation and divide acceptance.\nRemove div_wait, div_accept and in.valid from its capture enable and\nbubble-zero mux. On divide acceptance, the registered divider selector\nmakes the divider bank authoritative, so the simultaneously captured\nnormal result is inactive. Preserve saved post-forward divide operands\nin the accepting metadata and all existing resolved-PC/trap behavior.\nEach state bit must have exactly one procedural owner after the split.\n\nA memory stall must still freeze all EX/MEM payload, controls and bank\nselection, keeping address, write data and byte enables stable until\nacceptance. Keep mem_addr connected directly to the normal registered\nresult, without validity or divider-selection muxes on its output, so\nthe wrapper can still absorb its address register into block RAM.\nAn inactive address may change only when no memory request is owned.\nInvalid ID/EX and EX/MEM entries must retain zero control: downstream\nhazard, forwarding and memory logic currently rely on those controls,\nso stale payload must never assert a write, request, redirect or launch.\nKeep MEM/WB unchanged, including its deliberate retention of forwarding\ndata and reg_write metadata when a dmem hold clears retirement valid.\n\nExpect five percent higher fitness from shorter payload capture paths\nwith unchanged marker-bracketed instruction cycles. This is a prediction,\nnot a measured gain: capture-enable mapping, routing, the regfile read\ntree, ordinary ALU selection or divider recurrence may still limit Fmax.\nCheck the synthesized data/reset/enable cones to establish that bubble\nand completion decisions were actually removed from wide payload\nstorage; do not merely move those decisions to an output-side mux.\nInspect all three routed seeds and preserve the known timing-report\nlimitations rather than treating omitted arcs as zero delay.\n\nKeep nret=1, the external port set, decoder legality, all traps, ordered\nretirement, RV32M arithmetic and both real/ALTOPS schedules unchanged.\nRetain all correctness gates and formal depths. Run existing real and\nALTOPS unit suites, formal including liveness, stalled ISS cosimulation,\nUART/CRC/OOB/marker checks and the unchanged three-seed FPGA evaluation.\nUse identical binaries and stall schedules for cycle comparisons. The\nprior implementation notes distinguish a 2 KB evaluator workload from\nthe requested canonical 6 KB run; preserve that distinction and verify\nthe 6 KB CRCs without modifying the benchmark or evaluator contract.\n\nHYPOTHESIS_DIR True\nEXISTING_TARGET False\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
