{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,re\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=[json.loads(x) for x in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nfor r in rows:\n    if r['id']=='hyp-20260906-001-r11s0':\n        n=r.get('implementation_notes','')\n        print(n[-11000:])\nprint('\\\\nSHIFT/SHARE HISTORY MATCHES')\nfor r in rows:\n    h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n    s=h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else str(h)\n    for line in s.splitlines():\n        if re.search(r'shift|arithmetic.*shar|add.*sub.*shar|sign.inject',line,re.I): print(r['id'],line)\nprint('\\\\nFILE INVENTORY')\nfor d in ['cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses','cores/bench/test','.tmp/hyp-r13s0-validation/accepted/cores/bench/generated-homebrew']:\n    p=Path(d)\n    print(d, [x.name for x in p.iterdir()] if p.exists() else 'ABSENT')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,re\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=[json.loads(x) for x in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nfor r in rows:\n    if r['id']=='hyp-20260906-001-r11s0':\n        n=r.get('implementation_notes','')\n        print(n[-11000:])\nprint('\\\\nSHIFT/SHARE HISTORY MATCHES')\nfor r in rows:\n    h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n    s=h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else str(h)\n    for line in s.splitlines():\n        if re.search(r'shift|arithmetic.*shar|add.*sub.*shar|sign.inject',line,re.I): print(r['id'],line)\nprint('\\\\nFILE INVENTORY')\nfor d in ['cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses','cores/bench/test','.tmp/hyp-r13s0-validation/accepted/cores/bench/generated-homebrew']:\n    p=Path(d)\n    print(d, [x.name for x in p.iterdir()] if p.exists() else 'ABSENT')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"# Idle divider operand storage\n\nImplemented the hypothesis against starting winner `8357476ebbe4f81ec39bae4793d68a4eef9d0eac` (`hyp-20260906-002-r5s1`). Local correctness gates pass. The unchanged three-seed evaluator improves median Fmax from 184.06 to 184.84 MHz, or **0.423774856%**, with identical execution cycles.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- `cores/bench/rtl/div_unit.sv`: separated protocol/result ownership from the arithmetic storage, with synchronous reset and exactly one clocked owner per register. On pre-edge `!busy_q`, Q/R capture the existing four-bit magnitude prefix, and divisor, dividend, and all four flags capture current inputs regardless of request validity or a held response. Q/R advance on the existing seven recurrence edges and hold on the eighth correction edge. ALTOPS captures the unchanged selected subtraction/XOR expression on every idle edge and holds while busy.\n- `cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv`: retained the launch/accept state machine verbatim; moved RVFI snapshots to their own synchronous-reset process enabled only by `!div_active_q`. Snapshots retain the accepted operands through blocked completion and the acceptance edge, when EX/MEM samples their old values.\n- No arithmetic expressions, state declarations, pipeline stages, multiplier, normal memory-address bank, request qualification, forwarding priority, result-bank write conditions, or top-level ports changed. `nret` remains 1. Idle captures do not claim ownership, advance count, or produce responses.\n\nNo architectural deviation was required. The old ALU test assertion that arithmetic Q/R remained owned after completion was replaced with an assertion of the requested idle prefix capture. All response/result-bank stability assertions and all arithmetic, prefix, latency, reset, bubble, direct-address, and retirement checks remain.\n\n## Tests and equivalence\n\n- Requested Verilator lint passes with no warnings/errors, in real and ALTOPS modes.\n- Local `bash formal/run_all.sh`: **53 passed, 0 failed**, using unchanged single-retirement wrapper/config and ALTOPS. Environment: `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=6`, with the installed conda Python on PATH. The first configured proof run passed; no RTL formal fixes or retries were needed. The initial system-Python setup could not run the gate, so validation used the existing conda installation. Formal was staged under `$TMPDIR` to leave contract files untouched. Real-arithmetic `formal-deep` was not run; arithmetic expressions are unchanged, with real unit, ISS, and full-trace coverage below.\n- All nine pytest runners pass: real ALU 34 cocotb tests, ALTOPS ALU 34, real EX 5, ALTOPS EX 5, decoder 30, ID 1, immediate generator 8, pipeline 24, regfile 5; **146 cocotb tests total**.\n- Added changing idle operands/opcodes, exact different request-edge operands, busy input/request poisoning, captures beneath blocked responses, simultaneous consume/refill, and request/seventh-recurrence/terminal reset checks. EX tests cover all nine forwarding-source combinations, load-unavailable launch delays, memory holds, active snapshot retention, and a held EX/MEM divide owner surviving changing idle snapshots after ownership clears.\n- Added mixed pipeline streams with competing writers, all operand forwarding sources, retained WB load data, dependent and consecutive DIV/REM, immediate consumers, bus waits, redirects, and reset at request, recurrence, terminal, and completed-owner boundaries. Coverage assertions require the intended forwarding and overlap events. Initial test-only assertions were corrected on the starting RTL to include deliberate bus-hold cycles and avoid asking an aborted pre-launch scenario to consume a later hold schedule.\n- The identical protocol suite runs on the starting and candidate RTL. Optional `PIPELINE_TRACE_MODE=record` / `compare`, sharing `PIPELINE_TRACE_DIR`, records complete valid RVFI, bus schedules and accepted effects, accepted divide operands, dispatch results, resets, and cycle numbers. **34 scenarios, 28,706 sampled edges/events, 2,450 launches, and 5,814 retirements match exactly.** Each scenario also passes the unchanged Python ISS comparison. Existing one-clock ordinary/consumer and nine-clock consecutive-divide spacing checks pass; launch-to-accept remains eight clocks.\n- Unchanged `tools.eval.cosim.run_cosim` passes on both versions, including selftest and the evaluator's CoreMark configuration. Selftest additionally passes the unchanged ISS with both buses stalled using seeds 1, 2, 3, 19, and 97; all 115 retirements and their cycles match the starting RTL for each schedule.\n- The complete canonical 6 KB stalled CoreMark RVFI streams were compared byte for byte: **22,093,920 retirements and 6,463,986,468 bytes**, including every emitted retirement cycle and operand/result/memory field. No difference. Shared stream SHA256: `34ef03d244b986a66be40660efea1b01b6705ecbf1263bf493d109b7184ac4a0`.\n\n## FPGA evaluation and working-set discrepancy\n\nBoth versions used unchanged synthesis, wrapper, constraints, nextpnr script, seeds 1/2/3, and evaluator. All six routes completed. `make fpga TARGET=bench` used `NRET=1 BENCH=fpga/core_bench_si.sv`. The starting RTL reproduces the winner's recorded median and resource counts.\n\n| Metric | Starting | Candidate |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Seed 1 Fmax, MHz | 184.06 | 190.33 |\n| Seed 2 Fmax, MHz | 191.13 | 184.84 |\n| Seed 3 Fmax, MHz | 179.89 | 168.69 |\n| Median Fmax, MHz | 184.06 | 184.84 |\n| Evaluator bracketed cycles | 4,491,485 | 4,491,485 |\n| Exact evaluator iterations/cycle | 10 / 4,491,485 | 10 / 4,491,485 |\n| Evaluator fitness, iterations/s | 409.7976504430049 | 411.5342698461644 |\n| LUT4 | 5,490 | 5,485 |\n| Mapped FF | 2,112 | 2,119 |\n\nThe evaluator still builds **TOTAL_DATA_SIZE=2000**, `-O3`, ITERATIONS=10, and validates its existing 2 KB CRC table. This is a pre-existing discrepancy from the requested 6 KB contract; no evaluator or benchmark source was changed. Its unrounded iteration rate is `2.2264351322558128e-6`, not the rounded JSON field `2e-6`. Both versions ran the identical ELF, SHA256 `9b7d11c69a8a2b0db598fa2156474184488a3b2d22017f3fac05e6113ec74133`.\n\nSeparately built and validated the requested **TOTAL_DATA_SIZE=6000, -O3, ITERATIONS=10** configuration from unchanged sources, using the same ELF for both versions (SHA256 `f224290c528bdbc3caa7badb285d6b6ae1fab75523bde60110cefe80de23a9e4`). Both runs have:\n\n- Start marker cycle 56,393; stop marker cycle 32,893,064; **32,836,671 bracketed cycles**; final EBREAK cycle 32,900,232; no OOB access.\n- Exact iteration rate `10 / 32836671 = 3.0453757020618807e-7`.\n- CRCs `crclist=0xd4b0`, `crcmatrix=0xbe52`, `crcstate=0x5e47`, `seedcrc=0x8a02`, `crcfinal=0x5949`, and the literal `Correct operation validated.` UART message. UART and completion records match exactly.\n- Using the same routed medians gives separate 6 KB fitness **56.053185172150975 -> 56.290724476911805 iterations/s**. These numbers are not substituted into the unchanged evaluator's output.\n\nThe unchanged UART metadata reports `CoreMark Size: 2000` for the 6 KB run's per-algorithm share, and a hardcoded `-O2` compiler string. The actual build command used `-O3 -DTOTAL_DATA_SIZE=6000`; the canonical 6 KB CRCs identify the configuration.\n\n## Mapped D/CE cones\n\nInspected both mapped `synth.json` netlists, stopping combinational traversal at registered sources. Candidate enables were also evaluated over all busy/active/count combinations (320 mapped CE truth-table checks):\n\n- EX snapshots: `CE = !div_active_q`, one registered leaf, replacing a launch-qualified cone with 28 leaves.\n- Divisor, dividend, and four flags: `CE = !busy_q`, one registered leaf, replacing 28-leaf launch-qualified cones.\n- Q/R: `CE = !(busy_q && count_q == 7)`, four registered leaves, replacing 31-leaf qualified cones. Their D cones now select idle prefix versus recurrence using busy ownership and have no `div_active_q`/`held_q` request-state dependency. Arithmetic and forwarding data dependencies remain as intended.\n- `result_q` retains its four-leaf busy/count terminal enable. No idle-bank enable depends on held response ownership, opcode validity, load availability, request, or ready. Synchronous reset remains separate from these enables.\n\nNo RTL register was added, but mapping reports seven more physical FFs: two in each EX/MEM and MEM/WB register group and three under the register-file mapping. This physical resource increase is explicitly retained in the result rather than claiming an unchanged FF count.\n\n## All reported routed critical paths\n\nTimes below are nextpnr's printed path totals, rounded by that tool; Fmax above uses its final post-route frequency report. Cell names are the actual mapped endpoints, with architectural aliases verified against the mapped netlist.\n\n| Version/seed | Reported path | Total ns | Logic ns | Routing ns |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Starting 1 | EX/MEM `rd[0]` -> forwarding -> JALR target -> IF `pc[1]` | 5.43 | 3.06 | 2.38 |\n| Starting 2 | wrapper `lfsr[20]` -> decode/register-read selection -> ID/EX `rs2_val[3]` | 5.23 | 2.61 | 2.63 |\n| Starting 3 | EX/MEM `rd[0]` -> forwarding -> JALR target -> IF `pc[1]` | 5.56 | 3.06 | 2.50 |\n| Candidate 1 | ID/EX `alu_op[3]` -> normal ALU result selection -> normal address/result `[23]` | 5.25 | 2.35 | 2.90 |\n| Candidate 2 | MEM/WB `rd[1]` -> forwarding -> JALR target -> IF `pc[1]` | 5.41 | 2.86 | 2.55 |\n| Candidate 3 | ID/EX `alu_op[3]` -> normal ALU result selection -> normal address/result `[23]` | 5.93 | 2.35 | 3.58 |\n\nExact candidate endpoints:\n\n- Seeds 1 and 3: `cpu.u_id.reg_q_DFFRE_Q_162.Q` -> `cpu.u_ex.reg_q_DFFR_Q_72.D`.\n- Seed 2: `cpu.u_mem.reg_q_DFFR_Q_133.Q` -> `cpu.u_if.pc_DFFRE_Q.D`.\n\nExact starting endpoints:\n\n- Seeds 1 and 3: `cpu.u_ex.reg_q_DFFR_Q_22.Q` -> `cpu.u_if.pc_DFFRE_Q.D`.\n- Seed 2: `lfsr_DFFC_Q_10.Q` -> `cpu.u_id.reg_q_DFFRE_Q_124.D`.\n\nThese are the modeled paths reported by nextpnr. The absence of a divider endpoint does not establish divider timing margin or coverage of missing/unmodeled arcs. The small median gain cannot be attributed conclusively to a particular removed path; seed 3 regresses, and the two ALU-control paths differ substantially in routing delay. Additional idle switching is an explicit tradeoff and was not power-measured.\n\n## Evidence location\n\nAll scratch builds and evidence are under `$TMPDIR/divider-idle-r11s0/` (the run's existing `.tmp` directory), including `candidate/formal-local.log`, `candidate/units.log`, `candidate/remaining-tests.log`, `protocol-reference/`, `cosim-validation.json`, `sixk-validation.json`, `sixk-full-trace.json`, `fitness-comparison.json`, `mapped-cones.json`, both `fpga-eval.log` files, and all six extracted `*-critical-seed*.txt` reports. Contract files and other cores were not edited.\n\n\nSHIFT/SHARE HISTORY MATCHES\nhyp-20260906-002-r3s1 form 2D by a zero-extended shift of registered D. Compute 3D as an\nhyp-20260906-002-r3s1 explicitly widened shift plus add on the existing request edge, without\nhyp-20260906-002-r8s1 bank, divider latency/arithmetic, multiplier sharing, and all ALTOPS\nhyp-20260906-003-r11s2 the IF target adder. Retiming the exit path can still shift the worst\n\nFILE INVENTORY\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses ['.agent.hyp-20260906-002-r14s1.log', '.agent.hyp-20260906-003-r10s2.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-001-r11s0.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-001-r6s0.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-002-r3s1.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-001-r13s0.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-001-r8s0.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-003-r13s2.log', '.agent.hyp-20260906-002-r1s1.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-001-r4s0.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-003-r2s2.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-003-r12s2.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-002-r9s1.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-002-r5s1.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-002-r10s1.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-003-r14s2.log', '.agent.hyp-20260906-003-r6s2.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-003-r4s2.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-002-r12s1.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-003-r8s2.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-002-r7s1.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-001-r2s0.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-003-r12s2.log', '.agent.hyp-20260906-002-r13s1.log', '.agent.hyp-20260906-001-r7s0.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-002-r2s1.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-001-r10s0.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-003-r11s2.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-003-r1s2.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-003-r13s2.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-003-r3s2.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-001-r9s0.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-001-r5s0.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-001-r13s0.log', '.agent.hyp-20260906-001-r12s0.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-002-r11s1.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-003-r7s2.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-001-r14s0.log', '.agent.hyp-20260906-001-r1s0.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-002-r8s1.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-002-r4s1.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-001-r12s0.log', '.agent.hyp-20260906-002-r6s1.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-001-r3s0.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-003-r5s2.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-003-r9s2.last', '.agent.hyp-20260906-002-r13s1.last']\ncores/bench/test ['test_alu.py', 'conftest.py', 'test_decoder.py', 'test_imm_gen.py', 'test_id_stage.py', 'test_ex_result_banks.py', 'test_pipeline.py', '_helpers.py', 'test_reg_file.py']\n.tmp/hyp-r13s0-validation/accepted/cores/bench/generated-homebrew ['pnr_seed2', 'pnr_seed3', 'synth.json', 'pnr_seed1']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
