44:05 [liveness_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:03 (3)\\nSBY 12:44:05 [liveness_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\nSBY 12:44:05 [liveness_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: liveness_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 12:44:05 [liveness_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_liveness_check_sv_38_59 at rvfi_liveness_check.sv:38.5-38.28 step 20\\nSBY 12:44:05 [liveness_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/astra-max-20260905/bench-runs/gpt-6-astra_max-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260906-003-r6s2/formal/last_run-87052.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/astra-max-20260905/bench-runs/gpt-6-astra_max-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260906-003-r6s2/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-87052/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The current winner reaches 409.80 iter/sec at 184.06 MHz and 4,491,485\\nmarker-window cycles. The 16-entry predictor in r2s2 saved 6.135% of\\ncycles, but lost 13.074% of Fmax. Its routed paths included EX target\\nalignment and branch qualification feeding predictor payload enables.\\nStatic predictors in r3s2 through r5s2 also lost more frequency than\\nthey saved cycles; even control-only squashing left long recovery and\\nhazard paths. A predictor should move resolution off the same-cycle\\nrecovery and table-write paths while retaining the current winner's\\nindependent pipeline payload capture. The measured small-BTB cycle\\nbenefit makes delayed validation a worthwhile single predictor experiment.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Add one 16-entry direct-mapped bimodal BTB, and resolve prediction errors\\nfrom registered EX/MEM state in MEM. This moves recovery one cycle later\\nwithout adding a stage to ordinary instruction execution or retirement.\\nCorrect predictions still have no control-flow bubble; a misprediction\\ndiscards two younger slots instead of the existing one. The hypothesis\\nis that shorter recovery and training paths preserve enough Fmax to\\noutweigh that extra miss penalty.\\n\\nIndex the BTB with fetch PC[5:2], compare the full PC[31:6] tag, and store\\naligned target[31:2], a valid bit, and a two-bit saturating counter.\\nA valid tag hit with counter[1] set selects the stored target; otherwise\\nselect full-width PC+4. Legal conditional branches train direction;\\nJAL and JALR learn their latest aligned target and use counter 11.\\nReset clears validity; uninitialized payload must never affect a miss.\\nLookup depends only on PC and table state, without instruction predecode,\\nan instruction-immediate fetch adder, or stall/flush qualification in\\nthe target-select data cone. Keep imem_addr directly driven by the PC\\nregister. Prediction is applied only on actual fetch acceptance.\\n\\nCarry the exact consumed predicted_next_pc, lookup hit, and counter\\nsnapshot into ID/EX. Metadata follows the accepted instruction and\\nholds through load/decode holds, memory backpressure, and divider waits.\\nPreserve the winner's separation of payload capture from control/valid\\nclearing: dynamic squashes and invalid bubbles clear controls, while\\npayload flops retain their ordinary capture/hold enables. Metadata on\\ninvalid entries is inert. Lookup and a simultaneous table update use\\npre-edge table contents, with no combinational update bypass.\\n\\nEX continues computing architectural pc_next, including forwarded JALR,\\nPC+4 on the existing misalignment-trap continuation, and unchanged link\\nresults. Register the consumed predicted_next_pc alongside that actual\\npc_next in EX/MEM. Remove the immediate EX redirect. In MEM, compare\\nthese two registered full-width values for EVERY valid instruction,\\nincluding ordinary instructions, loads/stores, trapped instructions,\\nand completed DIV/REM with a stale BTB prediction. Assert repair only\\nwhen this EX/MEM owner can advance: valid, not reset, and no older dmem\\nhold. Drive repair_target directly from registered architectural\\npc_next. Do not put forwarded operands, live branch condition, target\\naddition, instruction legality, or div_wait in this comparison cone.\\nPreserve actual pc_next as the RVFI source. A held memory owner keeps\\nboth PCs until its first accepting edge; it must not consume a repair\\nor retire twice while blocked.\\n\\nA MEM repair wins over every younger fetch prediction and EX operation.\\nOn its accepting edge, redirect fetch even if imem is unavailable,\\ninvalidate the younger IF/ID slot and ID/EX entry, and inject a control-\\nzero invalid EX/MEM entry instead of accepting the younger EX result.\\nThe current MEM owner still advances normally into MEM/WB, including\\nits legitimate memory transaction and retirement. Add a younger-EX kill\\ninput that suppresses divider request/accept and effective div_wait on\\nthat repair cycle, and gives squash priority over the younger divide\\nhold. Do not reset the divider or its completion bank on repair: the\\nrepairing MEM owner can itself be a completed DIV/REM using that bank.\\nAn older memory hold already prevents a younger divide from launching;\\nonce the hold ends, pending MEM repair must kill it before launch.\\nCompute dmem hold independently of repair to avoid combinational loops.\\nWrong-path loads/stores must be killed before becoming memory owners.\\n\\nRetiming training is part of this same predictor. EX computes a small\\nupdate action and final counter from its accepted instruction and saved\\nlookup snapshot, then registers them with EX/MEM. Register the source\\nPC and target payload with ordinary payload enables, reusing existing\\nEX/MEM fields where possible. Only the registered action, registered\\nindex, and MEM-owner advancement may drive table write enables; no\\nsame-cycle EX outcome, target-alignment test, or generic EX-accept net\\nmay directly enable the wide BTB payload bank. An aligned conditional\\nhit saturates its saved counter and refreshes its direct target. An\\naligned taken conditional miss allocates at 10; a not-taken miss does\\nnothing. Legal aligned jumps write 11. Invalidate a saved hit for a\\nnon-control, illegal, or misaligned-target instruction, including an\\nuntaken conditional whose target is misaligned; never allocate it.\\nInvalid and killed owners have action NONE. Apply each registered action\\nonce on that owner's MEM advance, including the owner causing repair.\\nA stale snapshot may replace intervening state, but every allocation\\nwrites a coherent complete tag/target/counter tuple. Prediction errors\\nare always recoverable by the full-PC comparison.\\n\\nEstimate a 3% fitness improvement with low confidence. The earlier\\n6.135% cycle saving is evidence for early validation only; the extra\\nrecovery cycle must be measured, and may erase the benefit. A candidate\\nwith 3% fewer cycles breaks even at approximately 178.54 MHz against\\nthe current winner, and gains about 3.09% if Fmax stays at 184.06 MHz.\\nInspect all three routed seeds for MEM comparison-to-squash timing,\\nregistered-action-to-BTB enables, and unchanged raw load-use paths.\\nReport actual marker-window cycles, miss/recovery observations, median\\nFmax, LUT4/FF use, and net fitness. Preserve nret=1, all invariants,\\narithmetic/result-bank ownership, and the directly registered dmem\\naddress. Run unchanged lint, unit, formal, cosim, CRC/UART, OOB, marker,\\nresource, and three-seed FPGA gates. Prior logs identify a 2 KB versus\\n6 KB fixture discrepancy; keep evaluator results authoritative and any\\nseparate 6 KB measurement clearly supplemental without modifying either\\ncontract. This proposal changes only the bench predictor and its recovery.\\n\",\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"fitness_delta_pct\": 3,\n      \"confidence\": \"low\"\n    },\n    \"changes\": [\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Add the 16-entry fully tagged direct-mapped BTB with two-bit direction\\ncounters, PC-only lookup, valid-only reset, and synchronous writes\\ndriven exclusively by registered training records. Implement coherent\\nallocation, invalidation, and pre-edge lookup/update semantics.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Add consumed prediction and lookup-snapshot metadata to IF/ID and\\nID/EX, and predicted_next_pc plus the small registered training record\\nto EX/MEM. Reuse its existing actual pc_next and source PC. Keep all\\narchitectural controls, downstream RVFI fields, and nret=1 unchanged.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Select the raw BTB prediction for accepted PC advances and emit its\\nexact metadata. Preserve direct registered imem addressing, normal\\nstall behavior, invalid fetch bubbles, and reset/repair priority.\\nA prediction never squashes its producing instruction.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Capture prediction and lookup snapshots with instruction payload and\\nretain them across holds. Preserve independent payload capture and\\ncontrol-zero invalid bubbles so metadata adds no dynamic wide reset.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Preserve architectural resolution while registering predicted_pc and\\na training record with EX/MEM; remove same-cycle branch redirect.\\nAdd MEM-repair kill with control-zero younger EX/MEM squashing and\\ndivider-launch suppression, preserving the current MEM owner, held\\nforwarding data, divider completion bank, and direct mem_addr bank.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Wire PC-only predictor lookup and registered training. Generate MEM\\nrepair by comparing valid advancing EX/MEM actual/predicted PCs, use\\nits registered actual PC as target, and distribute repair to fetch,\\ndecode, and younger EX kill. Keep the external IO/RVFI shape intact.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Make MEM repair squash both younger stages and override younger\\ndivider holds, while deferring it through the current MEM owner's\\ndmem hold. Keep the dmem-stall equation independent of repair and\\npreserve load-use interlocking and retained MEM/WB forwarding data.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"test/test_branch_predictor.py\",\n        \"description\": \"Test full tags/targets, all counters, collision replacement, reset,\\ninvalidation, stale training snapshots, and simultaneous lookup/write.\\nCheck that inactive or held update records never train repeatedly.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n        \"description\": \"Verify zero-bubble warm predictions and two-slot miss recovery with\\ncomplete RVFI comparison against the unchanged ISS. Cover direction\\nand target mistakes, changing JALR targets, loop exits, stale hits on\\nordinary/memory/divide/illegal instructions, alignment traps, long\\ndmem holds, imem unavailability, load forwarding, consecutive repairs,\\nand reset. Observe actual accepted stores and divider launches to\\nprove MEM repair kills younger work before any side effect, including\\na younger divide on the memory-release edge and a repairing DIV/REM\\nowner whose registered completion must still retire correctly.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"test/test_id_stage.py\",\n        \"description\": \"Extend bundle constructors and metadata capture/hold checks. Retain\\nassertions that squashes clear all controls without governing wide\\npayload capture and that invalid metadata cannot enable any action.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"test/test_ex_result_banks.py\",\n        \"description\": \"Update packed bundles and default the new kill input low in existing\\ntests. Add recovery-edge ownership checks without weakening divider,\\nforwarding, reset, or directly registered memory-address assertions.\\n\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"implementation_notes\": null\n}\nhyp-20260906-003-r7s2\nImplemented the single-entry backedge predictor as specified. Correctness gates pass, but the measured timing loss rejects the forecasted fitness gain: the unchanged local evaluator reports 115.85 MHz median and 268.66 iter/sec, versus the supplied winner's 184.06 MHz and 409.80 iter/sec. These are approximately 37.06% lower Fmax and 34.44% lower fitness. No acceptance decision or evaluator record was changed.\n\n- Added branch_predictor.sv with one valid bit, 30 source bits, 30 target bits, and the complete 12-bit B displacement. Synthesis retains all 73 entry flops. Only validity resets; reset cancels a pending payload write. Miss outputs are zero. Lookup requires exact source equality and word alignment, uses full addresses, and has no update bypass.\n- IF selects the raw lookup target versus full-width PC+4. Reset and existing EX repair have priority; normal advancement requires fetch acceptance. imem_addr still comes directly from the PC register. A prediction does not flush its own instruction.\n- IF/ID carries the lookup-use bit and displacement snapshot. ID compares every B displacement bit against a current legal branch decode, preserving architectural branch_op and source-register fields. ID/EX carries prediction_used, certified_backedge, and branch_op[0] XOR certified_backedge as registered repair polarity. Invalid/flush controls are inert, holds retain all owner metadata, and independent payload capture remains intact.\n- EX shares equality/signed-less-than/unsigned-less-than predicates between actual branch resolution and the decode-folded repair polarity. No prediction uses ordinary EX recovery; certified predictions repair only false outcomes to PC+4; stale predictions always repair to the current architectural next PC, including illegal encodings, alignment traps, memory operations, and DIV/REM. The exceptional actual-next-PC selection remains separate from the ordinary redirect and certified-exit selections. RVFI always carries the actual next PC.\n- EX repair is qualified by valid and reset, with no new EX-accept/div_wait gate. The unchanged hazard priority retains held memory/divider owners and clears only the younger combinational slot when the owner advances. Trapped jumps still suppress link writes.\n- A registered train_pending pulse is generated only for an accepted legal aligned taken negative-displacement conditional branch. It clears on every other clock, including holds. The following edge writes the existing EX/MEM pc, branch_target and instruction displacement. There is no additional training payload bank, resident-state feedback, or live EX/memory-ready write enable.\n\nNo architectural deviations were needed. The decoder, arithmetic/divider implementation, divider completion bank, retained WB forwarding, hazard priority, directly registered dmem address, and nret=1 external port set are unchanged. Test-only additions include dynamic instruction versions and optional marker-window counters; there are no hardware event counters, workload PC constants, address truncations, new prediction classes, or evaluator/formal-bound changes.\n\n- Requested verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv: PASS, no warnings.\n- Unchanged RVFI channel-0 pattern gate: PASS.\n- Unit suite: 10 pytest runners pass. Final XML aggregate: 153 cocotb cases pass; the optional CoreMark measurement is skipped in normal runs and was also run separately to completion. Both real and ALTOPS arithmetic/result-bank tests pass. The final pipeline-only rerun after adding reset coverage passes.\n- Directed coverage includes all tag/target bits, all displacement comparison bits, page crossings and modulo-2^32 wraparound, pre-edge lookup/write collisions, valid-only reset and canceled pending writes, once-per-owner staged training across holds, nested eviction, and cold/warm/exit timing. Warm-loop branch-to-successor gaps are exactly [2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2] clocks.\n- Full RVFI comparison against the unchanged ISS passes for changed displacements, all six branch conditions and changed registers, forwarded loaded operands, ALU/multiply, legal and misaligned loads/stores/JAL/JALR, illegal instructions, and DIV/REM replacements. Independent accepted bus request and divider launch checks catch wrong-path effects and duplication. Long memory holds, unavailable imem, consecutive repairs, completion holds, and reset of a hot entry plus a stale dividing owner pass.\n- Local formal status: PASS on the first RTL attempt, 53 checks passed and 0 failed, including liveness, pc_fwd/pc_bwd, unique, ill, and cover. No counterexample and no formal fix/retry were needed. The exact unchanged run_all.sh/checks_si.cfg/wrapper_si.sv were run in an isolated scratch copy with RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=6. Actual divider arithmetic remains covered by real unit tests and cosim; formal-deep was not run because divider arithmetic was unchanged.\n- Unchanged make cosim TARGET=bench: PASS, both selftest full-trace ISS comparison and CoreMark CRC validation.\n- Unchanged make fpga TARGET=bench with NRET=1 and BENCH=fpga/core_bench_si.sv: all three seeds route successfully. An initial invocation selected Makefile's default two-channel synthesis wrapper and stopped before routing; rerunning with the existing declared single-channel wrapper resolved that setup mismatch without modifying the contract.\n\nAll three routed seeds were inspected, including the existing forwarding/JALR/alignment paths displaced by routing. Each worst path passes through forwarding and low JALR target alignment, then repair/hold/squash logic, ending at an ID control RESET pin. Seed 1 begins at ID state; seeds 2 and 3 begin at retained MEM/WB instruction/register-address bits. The predictor tag-to-PC path remains present through eight mapped combinational cells including muxes and a packing passthrough. This is a structural depth count, not an isolated path-period measurement. PC data endpoints were also inspected in each detailed timing report.\n\nThe predictor payload CE cone was checked in every routed netlist: all 72 payload flops share a single LUT2 driven only by registered train_pending and reset. Validity is enabled directly by train_pending. There is no live EX comparator, resident match, or memory-ready input to those enables. Detailed reports contain the training-pulse D and validity-CE endpoint arrivals; the full payload-enable connectivity was checked separately. No claim is made that this wide physical net is free of routing cost.\n\nOptional unit-harness CoreMark counters used the unchanged ELF and the exact C++ harness xorshift stall sequence. The measured start/stop cycles were 15,666 and 4,327,733, reproducing the evaluator's 4,312,067-cycle window exactly:\n\n| Marker-window event | Count |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Useful certified taken hits | 192,341 |\n| Certified loop-exit repairs | 12,211 |\n| Stale repairs | 0 |\n| Ordinary repairs | 165,186 |\n| Staged entry writes | 235,191 |\n| Entry replacements (resident tuple changed) | 42,850 |\n\nValidation artifacts are preserved under /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/astra-max-20260905/bench-runs/gpt-6-astra_max-rep2/.tmp/r7s2-validation-_8mhz1xm. Relevant files are formal-gate.log, formal/last_run-15123.log, cosim-gate.log, fpga-gate.log, predictor-counts.json, predictor-measurement.log, sixkb-build.log, sixkb-coremark.log, timing-inspection.json, routed-cone-inspection.json, and cores/bench/generated/pnr_seed{1,2,3}/{nextpnr.log,timing.json,timing-full.log}. Unit logs are under $TMPDIR/r7s2-unit-tests-final.log and $TMPDIR/r7s2-pipeline-final.log. Scratch contract copies and generated outputs stay under $TMPDIR; no protected worktree files or other cores were changed.\n\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ls -la cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses | tail -7; sed -n '1,140p' formal/checks_si.cfg; sed -n '1,180p' formal/riscv-formal/checks/rvfi_liveness_check.sv; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport importlib.util\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor s in ['yaml','jsonschema']:\n    print(s, bool(importlib.util.find_spec(s)))\nfor p in [Path('/opt/miniconda3'),Path('/opt/anaconda3'),Path('/Users/bonetto/miniconda3'),Path('.tmp/r11s2-validation/cores/bench/sim_build/prediction_profile/prediction-counters.json')]:\n    print(p, p.exists())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ls -la cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses | tail -7; sed -n '1,140p' formal/checks_si.cfg; sed -n '1,180p' formal/riscv-formal/checks/rvfi_liveness_check.sv; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport importlib.util\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor s in ['yaml','jsonschema']:\n    print(s, bool(importlib.util.find_spec(s)))\nfor p in [Path('/opt/miniconda3'),Path('/opt/anaconda3'),Path('/Users/bonetto/miniconda3'),Path('.tmp/r11s2-validation/cores/bench/sim_build/prediction_profile/prediction-counters.json')]:\n    print(p, p.exists())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"-rw-r--r--@  1 bonetto  staff     356 Sep  6 10:25 .agent.hyp-20260906-003-r3s2.last\n-rw-r--r--@  1 bonetto  staff     354 Sep  6 11:01 .agent.hyp-20260906-003-r4s2.last\n-rw-r--r--@  1 bonetto  staff     374 Sep  6 11:44 .agent.hyp-20260906-003-r5s2.last\n-rw-r--r--@  1 bonetto  staff     346 Sep  6 12:16 .agent.hyp-20260906-003-r6s2.last\n-rw-r--r--@  1 bonetto  staff     357 Sep  6 12:59 .agent.hyp-20260906-003-r7s2.last\n-rw-r--r--@  1 bonetto  staff     341 Sep  6 13:39 .agent.hyp-20260906-003-r8s2.last\n-rw-r--r--@  1 bonetto  staff     342 Sep  6 14:22 .agent.hyp-20260906-003-r9s2.last\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n// Copyright (C) 2017  Claire Xenia Wolf <claire@yosyshq.com>\n//\n// Permission to use, copy, modify, and/or distribute this software for any\n// purpose with or without fee is hereby granted, provided that the above\n// copyright notice and this permission notice appear in all copies.\n//\n// THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\" AND THE AUTHOR DISCLAIMS ALL WARRANTIES\n// WITH REGARD TO THIS SOFTWARE INCLUDING ALL IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF\n// MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHOR BE LIABLE FOR\n// ANY SPECIAL, DIRECT, INDIRECT, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES OR ANY DAMAGES\n// WHATSOEVER RESULTING FROM LOSS OF USE, DATA OR PROFITS, WHETHER IN AN\n// ACTION OF CONTRACT, NEGLIGENCE OR OTHER TORTIOUS ACTION, ARISING OUT OF\n// OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE USE OR PERFORMANCE OF THIS SOFTWARE.\n\nmodule rvfi_liveness_check (\n\tinput clock, reset, trig, check,\n\t`RVFI_INPUTS\n);\n\t`rvformal_rand_const_reg [63:0] insn_order;\n\treg found_next_insn = 0;\n\n\tinteger channel_idx;\n\talways @(posedge clock) begin\n\t\tif (reset) begin\n\t\t\tfound_next_insn = 0;\n\t\tend else begin\n\t\t\tfor (channel_idx = 0; channel_idx < `RISCV_FORMAL_NRET; channel_idx=channel_idx+1) begin\n\t\t\t\tif (rvfi_valid[channel_idx] && rvfi_order[64*channel_idx +: 64] == insn_order+1) begin\n\t\t\t\t\tfound_next_insn = 1;\n\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\tend\n\t\t\tif (trig) begin\n\t\t\t\tassume(rvfi_valid[`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX]);\n\t\t\t\tassume(!rvfi_halt[`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX]);\n\t\t\t\tassume(insn_order == rvfi_order[64*`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX +: 64]);\n\t\t\tend\n\t\t\tif (check) begin\n\t\t\t\tassert(found_next_insn);\n\t\t\tend\n\t\tend\n\tend\nendmodule\nyaml False\njsonschema False\n/opt/miniconda3 False\n/opt/anaconda3 False\n/Users/bonetto/miniconda3 False\n.tmp/r11s2-validation/cores/bench/sim_build/prediction_profile/prediction-counters.json True\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
